{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TPynqn6c8NbnQM8cyiUQMS","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# script-analysis — technique log (days 1-25; updated after every day)\n2\t\n3\tHow this lane has looked so far (these are observations, not guarantees):\n4\t- **Timed variants MUTATE** (organizer, Day 8: \"new, dynamic variations/mutations ... new unseen effects\"): nothing below is a\n5\t  guarantee for Time Trial / Mastery -- solvers derive structure and degrade per field. **D23 proved it hard: the timed\n6\t  contract had a DIFFERENT SHAPE from the single** (hashed member names, per-file ids, composite fields, `LYR-` carrier tags;\n7\t  see Variant axes) -- the carried solver answered only 593/1495 TT ids.\n8\t- One AES zip `evidence.zip` (password `infected`) of inert \"Huntress Script Triage\" fixtures. **The single contract is\n9\t  CUMULATIVE**: each day keeps every earlier file/question and adds one language; bytes and values re-roll daily. PS (d1, 15\n10\t  ids) -> +JScript (d2, 87) -> +Batch (d3) -> +VBScript (d4) -> +Python (d5, 357) -> +Bash (d6) -> +Node `.mjs` + Bash advanced\n11\t  (d7, 469) -> +PHP + WSF/HTA/webshell hosts (d8, 615) -> +Lua/SCT/OpenResty (d9) -> MOF (d10) -> TypeScript (d11) -> AutoIt\n12\t  (d12) -> AppleScript (d13) -> MSBuild `.proj` (d14, 971) -> Perl + perl_cgi (d15) -> Ruby + ruby_rack (d16, 1095) ->\n13\t  AutoHotkey (d17) -> Apps Script + google_docs_sidebar (d18) -> C# `.csx` + ASPX (d19, 1249) -> Groovy + jenkins_pipeline +\n14\t  classic_asp + 2 Bash (d20, 1329) -> GitHub Actions `.yml` (d21, 1373) -> NSIS `.nsi` (d22, 1417) -> GDScript `.gd` (d23,\n15\t  1461 = +44, no host) -> JSP `.jsp` (d24, 1516 = +55, 4 polyglots + `host-jsp-webshell-jsp`) -> **Elixir `.exs` (d25, 1571 =\n16\t  +55, 167 members: 4 polyglots + `host-elixir-phoenix-elixir`)**. Bash advanced +2 most days (not d12, d15, d17-d19, d21-d23). Since D8 the\n17\t  TITLE/PROMPT is a pun; the new language shows up only in the member list (D16 \"Same Same, But Different\" -> Ruby; D19 \"Sharp\n18\t  Practice\" -> C#; D20 \"The Butler Did It\" -> Jenkins/Groovy; D21 \"Actions Speak Louder\" -> GHA; D22 \"Next, Next, Finish\" ->\n19\t  NSIS; D23 \"Press Start to Decode\" / base `game-resource-loader` -> Godot GDScript; D24 \"Web of Lies\" / base\n20\t  `jsp-webshell-source` -> JSP; **D25 \"Ashes to Assets\" (phoenix pun) / base `phoenix-stage-chain` -> Elixir + Phoenix host;\n21\t  the prompt NAMED the language for the first time**). Diff contract ids against yesterday's.\n22\t- **Forecast cue (D24, CONFIRMED D25)**: the timed plans' `next_language` pool holds only never-shipped languages; each day's\n23\t  new language leaves it. D23 pool had `jsp` -> D24 shipped JSP; D24 pool had `elixir` -> D25 shipped Elixir and the D25 pool\n24\t  lost exactly `elixir`. Remaining 15 = awk, beanshell, dockerfile, erlang, fish, kotlin, makefile, nim, rust, sed, swift,\n25\t  tcl, terraform_hcl, xslt, zsh (6 days left, so ~9 will never ship). Rebuild it nightly from the auto-* expected.json.\n26\t- From day 2 on, every fixture hides a **self-describing plan**: `v=N|steps=a,b|adapter=..|stage_count=..|campaign_id=..|<indicators>`.\n27\t  It sits behind a codec, usually named in a `Codec_<id>` / `CODEC_<id>` / `rem HUNTRESS-CODEC:` const of the form `rep|transform|key`.\n28\t  Most exact_text answers are plan values copied verbatim. From D8 there is also a **`v=3` plan**: it carries `role=` and `attack=`\n29\t  itself, and sits behind a `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<TAG>-` comment.\n30\t- The hard part is **naming CODE SHAPE**: control-flow, expansion, and function/invocation/property styles. These are GM synthetic\n31\t  labels that are not in the plan. Role and scenario are enums, so read `accepted_values`.\n32\t- Single-solve files are named by behaviour (host-context, memory-stage, embedded-write, remote-write, local-dispatch,\n33\t  staged-handoff, outbound-transfer, impact-plan, relay-handoff); answer-id = `<lang>-<role>-<field>`. **Timed D23: members are\n34\t  `<6hex>.<ext>` and ids `<family>-<6hex>-<field>`** -- no behaviour name anywhere; role comes from the plan only.\n35\t- Narrative prompts (D8 siblings, D15 phantom store, D16 equivalence, D17 network reconcile, D18 process tree, D19 bridge, D20\n36\t  controller/agent, D21 trust boundary, D22 setup-vs-payload, D23 \"the level that doesn't belong\", D24 \"order of requests and stages,\n37\t  inert fixture vs real execution primitives\", D25 \"follow every transformation ... the setting that didn't survive the\n38\t  rebirth\") have NEVER been asked as an outlier/compare question. D23's \"correlate with the corpus\"\n39\t  did surface ONCE as a cross-file id: `python-<6hex>-handoff-id` = the `$HandoffId` the PowerShell precursor passes to that .py.\n40\t- Time Trial windows ~5-17 s when the solver fits. Mastery = `setN.` ids; 2 sets d2-d7/d10-d14, 5 sets d8-d9/d15-d21, 6 sets\n41\t  D22 (8502), 7 sets D23 (10465), 8 sets D24 (12480), **9 sets D25 (14625 = 9 x 1625)** -- +1 set/day since D21 -- in one outer `evidence-01.zip` holding `evidence-01..07.zip`; the set loop is\n42\t  count-agnostic. Same-named deliveries: pair by sha256. Timed questions carry `[assigned-artifact-sha256:<hex>]`. From D15 the\n43\t  timed contracts are the untimed regular pool (`run_for_time:false`, `variant_fresh:true`, no deadline).\n44\t\n45\t## Variant axes (what differs between the single, Time Trial and Mastery variants of the SAME day -- parse every value listed)\n46\tEach miss cost one failed timed attempt + a generalize cycle (D6: 4 cycles; D7: 1; D8-D14: 0; D15: 1; D16-D22: 0). **D23: TT\n47\t5 generalize workers, Mastery 3 -- ~14 min + ~11 min to CORRECT**; D24-D25: 0 (per-file shape persisted, solver fit). Auto cases\n48\tD20-D22 (TT 717b8371/f01e0ff9/c355207f, M 1478867c/2620b793/c8d60ca4), D24 (TT 1c3f64b8, M 2afec5c3) and D25 (TT b59af3dd,\n49\tM 9fd70fc3) are value re-rolls;\n50\tD23 TT b10c4da4 / M e24c070d carry the new shape.\n51\t- **CONTRACT SHAPE (D23 NEW; single vs timed)** -- single: semantic ids `<lang>-<role>-<field>` over behaviour-named members\n52\t  (1461). Timed: members renamed `<6hex>.<ext>`, ids `<family>-<6hex>-<field>` (families `powershell`, `jscript`, `batch`,\n53\t  `vbscript`, `python`, `bash`, `bash-advanced`, `nodejs`, `polyglot-<lang>` incl. `polyglot-javascript/jscript/vbscript` for\n54\t  the hosts). New/changed fields: **composite `style`** = labels joined by `|` (JS `function|invocation|property`; batch\n55\t  `graph|control|expansion`; VBS `representation|transform|control`); python `carrier` = `carrier|windows_chain`, python\n56\t  `obfuscation` = `syntax|obfuscation`; **`indicator`** = FIRST plan indicator present in the question's order (url, upload_url,\n57\t  next_stage, file_path, schedule_path, note/recovery-note name, host_id); **`campaign-token`** = campaign after its first\n58\t  hyphen; **`url-host`** = hostname of the plan url; **`path-leaf`** = last segment of file_path; PS `url`/`secondary`/\n59\t  `tertiary` chosen by scenario (resource: wallet/mutex; collection: staged file/UA; impact: note/extension); python\n60\t  **`handoff-id`** (cross-file, below). Parse rule: match `^(?P<fam>.+?)-(?P<stem>[0-9a-f]{6})-(?P<field>[a-z][a-z0-9-]*)$`,\n61\t  require stem == member stem, route by field name; READ the question text for join order / precedence -- it states both.\n62\t  Diff a timed contract's id SHAPE against the single's before trusting the carried solver (D23 solve.py `PF_ID`/`pf_value`).\n63\t  **D24: same grammar again** (TT 1560 = 1495 + 65); the new language joins as `polyglot-jsp` x 5 members x 13 fields (role,\n64\t  attack, steps, stage-count, stage-profile, obfuscation, next-language, campaign, url, file-path, url-host, path-leaf,\n65\t  campaign-token) -- the single's `host-jsp-webshell-jsp` is NOT a separate family in timed (no host-profile field asked).\n66\t  **D25: unchanged again** (TT 1625 = 1560 + 65): `polyglot-elixir` x 5 members x the same 13 fields; the single's\n67\t  `host-elixir-phoenix-elixir` folds into it the same way. Rule held: a new language = +65 timed ids in one `polyglot-<lang>`.\n68\t- **Plan carrier tag (v=3)** -- D8-D22 `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<TAG>-<data>` with tags `B64`/`HEX`/`HB64`/`FRAG` (= obfuscation\n69\t  profile base64/plain_hex/hex_base64/fragmented_hex), fixed per file in every delivery. D18 `SPLIT` = layout tag (no data;\n70\t  the data is the next multi-line `[..].join(\"\")` array). **D23 timed: `LYR-<l1>_<l2>[_<l3>]-<data>`**, layers from {`b64`,\n71\t  `b32`, `hex`, `rev`, `frag`} in ENCODE order (decode last-first: frag = drop `.`, rev = reverse, b32 = upper+pad); the\n72\t  obfuscation answer is the layer string itself (`hex_hex_hex`, `b64_b32`, `b32_rev`, 54 distinct seen). Apps Script splits the\n73\t  LYR string across an array -> join first, then LYR-peel. The single still used B64/HEX/HB64/FRAG. Parse rule: tag-directed\n74\t  peel when the tag parses as a layer list, else shape peel (max 4 layers); accept only `v=`.\n75\t  D24-D25 timed: same 5 layer names (D25 e.g. `hex_b64_b32`, `hex_b32`); no new layer name in 3 days.\n76\t- **Plan VOCABULARY re-roll (D23-D24 timed)** -- stage_profile `<colour>_<shape>` (amber/cobalt/ivory/onyx/ruby/slate/teal/umber x\n77\t  braid/ladder/lattice/pivot/spindle/weave), next_language anything (awk, beanshell, dockerfile, elixir, erlang, fish, jsp,\n78\t  kotlin, makefile, nim, rust, sed, swift, tcl, terraform_hcl, xslt, zsh; D24 minus jsp; D25 minus elixir), stage_count 2-8, timed polyglot\n79\t  roles span all 8 (persistence_descriptor/T1053, uploader/T1041, dropper/T1140, stager/T1105 included), python syntax/obfuscation new\n80\t  (match_case, walrus_binding, class_staticmethod, marshal_envelope_plan, closure_cells, string_table, lambda_indirection).\n81\t  Parse rule: plan-verbatim; never validate plan values against a known list.\n82\t- **GM label regime (batch `expansion`)** -- SAME bytes, DIFFERENT label by key. Old regime (D3-D14 + D15 single): whole\n83\t  handoff, `echo(!var!)` => delayed unless a FOR/h-pool rule fires. Statement regime (D15 timed, D16+ every mode; `run_for_time\n84\t  is False` OR `started_at >= 2026-10-16`; `lib.codec.label_regime`): label the JOIN STATEMENT -- `!a!!b!` = delayed; `for ..\n85\t  do call set` = for_indirect; bare `call set \"x=%%h0%%..\"` = call_double; `call set` over other pools = percent; plain `set\n86\t  \"x=%a%%b%\"` = percent. **D23 FIELD-keyed: inside the composite `-style` triple a `call set \"..%%x%%..\"` second pass is\n87\t  `call_double` on ANY pool** (TT b10c4da4 4 ids, Mastery e24c070d 12 ids rejected as `percent`), while the stand-alone\n88\t  `-expansion` field keeps `percent` for the same construct. When byte-identical constructs get different labels, tabulate\n89\t  (construct, label) against EVERY contract key (started_at, run_for_time, variant_fresh) AND the asking field at once.\n90\t- **Mastery set scoping (D23)** -- the same member stem (`4c1097.py`) recurs in all 7 sets with a different precursor value per\n91\t  set; a cross-file lookup indexed over the whole bundle returned set1's handoff id for sets 2-7 (6 rejected). Parse rule: index\n92\t  and resolve cross-file references PER SET (inner `evidence-0N.zip`), never per outer artifact. D24-D25: stems again identical\n93\t  across all sets (`588efb.jsp`, `a7470f.exs` in set1..set9) with set-distinct plans.\n94\t- **Codec per file** -- rep x transform x key re-roll per variant; NEW rep names appear only on variants (D7 TT\n95\t  `unicode_escapes`, `json_numbers`, `reversed_base64`, Bash `xor_hex|cd`). Decode by material SHAPE x named transform; accept\n96\t  only `v=`. Spec arity: `rep|transform|key`, `rep|` (empty = identity), or transform folded into the rep (`xor_hex|cd`).\n97\t- **Plan carrier NESTING (D10 MOF, D19 ASPX)** -- inner script as an escaped string of the host; unescape (`\\n \\\" \\\\`, `\"\"`,\n98\t  `&quot;`/CDATA, `\"`) and rescan; call `lib.codec.v3_plan` before anything else.\n99\t- **Plan carrier host syntax (v=3)** -- marker in the host's comment: `//`, `--`, `;`, `<!-- -->`, `#` (Perl, Ruby, YAML,\n100\t  **GDScript**), `'` in `<% %>`. Descriptor forms: `$descriptor_<id>`, `var/local/const/final String/my descriptor_<id> =`,\n101\t  AutoIt `Global Const`, AppleScript `property ..:`, AHK `:=`, Ruby `DESCRIPTOR_<8HEX> =`, `<HuntressDescriptor>`, ASP `Dim`\n102\t  then assign, builder maps, YAML `env: HUNTRESS_DESCRIPTOR:` (no id), NSIS `StrCpy $0 \"..\"` (no name), **GDScript typed const\n103\t  `const DESCRIPTOR_<8HEX>: String = \"..\"`** (type annotation between name and `=`). Parse rule: regex the MARKER\n104\t  `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V\\d+\\s*:\\s*(\\w*)-?\\s*([^\\s\"'<>\\]]+)` over raw bytes; never anchor on `=`/`:=`/`set`/`<-`.\n105\t  D25 Elixir: `#` marker + a plain lowercase binding `descriptor_<8hex> = \"..\"` (NOT the forecast `@descriptor` attribute or a\n106\t  `~s()` sigil) + `_plan_<8hex> = %{descriptor: ..}` map.\n107\t- **Literal shapes (D6-D7)** -- radix from the code; base64 std AND urlsafe; reverse the LIST vs the TEXT (try both); join\n108\t  split chunks / `+=` / adjacent strings / `.`-FRAG / `[..].join(\"\")` first; carriers may be frozen exes (D6 cx_Freeze).\n109\t- **Transport/runner, not variant** -- D7 TT `{\"error\":\"rate_limited\"}` saved as the zip; D8 TT 503; D16 60 s runner cap; D23\n110\t  one TT generalize worker died \"Prompt is too long\" (1.39 M tokens: the 1495-id contract + artifacts inlined). Never harvest\n111\t  these as cases.\n112\t\n113\t## Recognition cues -> first move\n114\t| You see | First move |\n115\t|---|---|\n116\t| `evidence.zip`, \"method=AES Encrypted\" | Triage already extracted it (`work/extracted/`) and decoded every plan. Diff the member list / contract ids against yesterday's to find the new language. Open members with `lib.common.read_member` (zipfile can't read AES). |\n117\t| Prior-day languages in the contract | Cumulative: rerun the carried marker-routed solver FIRST (D9-D23 single: it covered each new v=3 language unchanged except D18/D19 carrier patches). Any planless file: `lib.codec.v3_plan(text)`. Spend thinking on the new language and on label regimes. |\n118\t| **Timed contract ids `<family>-<6hex>-<field>`, members `<6hex>.<ext>` (D23)** | Contract-shape change, not a decode failure. Count ids answered vs asked FIRST; route by `PF_ID` + field name; composite fields join with `\\|` in the question's order; indicator by the question's precedence list; resolve cross-file ids (`handoff-id`) per set. |\n119\t| `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:LYR-<l>_<l>-..` (D23 timed) | Tag = encode layers (b64/b32/hex/rev/frag); undo last-first; obfuscation answer = the layer string verbatim. |\n120\t| `.ps1` `$encodedMaterial = [Convert]::FromBase64String('..')` + `$nativeTypes` | `base64 -d` -> JSON descriptor: url/wallet/mutex/UA/file/ext/note by SHAPE. `$nativeTypes`: Process/Registry+wallet=resource, ZipFile/HttpWebRequest=collection, Aes/DirectoryInfo=impact. `invoke-python-stage.ps1` carries `$HandoffId = 'PSPY-<16HEX>'` + `$NextStage`. |\n121\t| `.js` WSH, `decode_*`/`recover_*`/`inspect_*`, XOR key arrays | Run each file in an empty `node` `vm` (no require/ActiveXObject, `eval` -> capture); keep the first object with `steps`. Styles from the `inspect_*` body. |\n122\t| `.bat/.cmd` `rem HUNTRESS-CODEC:` / `set \"itemN=..` / `:HUNTRESS_INSPECT` | Plan in `set` fragments; emulate cmd expansion in Python. Expansion label: statement regime, but `call set %%x%%` inside a `-style` triple = call_double (Variant axes). Never run cmd. |\n123\t| `.vbs` `Const Material_<id>`, `Const Codec_<id> = \"rep|transform|key\"` | Decode from the Codec const; rep/transform = Codec fields 1/2 verbatim. Control = construct wrapping `Decode_` inside `Recover_`. |\n124\t| `.py` `*-recovered.py` with `MATERIAL_<id>`, `CODEC_<id>` | Decode from CODEC (or AST-whitelisted `decode_(load_(..))`). Plan v=2 carries syntax/obfuscation/carrier/windows_chain verbatim. |\n125\t| `.sh` `readonly Material_<id>` + `readonly Codec_<id>` (+ `Feature_<id>()`) | Decode from the Codec const (multi-byte key = COMMA list). `Feature_` fixtures: role `advanced_syntax`, feature/primitive/campaign/stage_count/steps plan-verbatim, T1059.004. Never run bash. |\n126\t| `.mjs` ESM `const Material_<id>`, async `load_/decode_/recover_/inspect_/plan_<id>` | Static decode (`lib.codec.find_codecs` + shape fallback). Plan fields verbatim. |\n127\t| `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<TAG>-..` in any comment + a descriptor literal (`.php .lua .js .vbs .mof .ts .au3 .applescript .proj .pl .rb .ahk .gs .csx .groovy .yml .nsi .gd`) | **Route by the marker before the extension.** Peel to `v=3|language=..|role=..|attack=..|adapter=..|host_profile=..|obfuscation_profile=..|stage_profile=..|next_language=..|stage_count=..|steps=..|campaign_id=..|url=..|file_path=..`. EVERY answer incl. role/attack is plan-verbatim. |\n128\t| `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:SPLIT` (no data) + `const HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1_SPLIT_<id> = [..].join(\"\")` (D18) | Join the array literals, drop the `<TAG>-` head, peel. 44 new ids unanswered = CARRIER bug; never walk the role enum. |\n129\t| ASPX `<script runat=\"server\">` + `EmbeddedCsx_<id> = \"// HUNTRESS..\\n..\\\"..\\\";\"` (D19) | NESTED carrier: unescape `\\n`/`\\\"`/`\\\\` (and `\"\"`, `&quot;`, CDATA) and rescan; `lib.codec.v3_plan` does. |\n130\t| New language, plain one-line marker: `.csx` (D19), `.groovy` (D20), `.yml` (D21 `env: HUNTRESS_DESCRIPTOR`), `.nsi` (D22 `StrCpy $0`), `.exs` (D25, next row), **`.gd` (D23: line-1 `# HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<TAG>-..`, `extends RefCounted`, `const DESCRIPTOR_<8HEX>: String = \"..\"`, `func build_plan_<id>() -> Dictionary: return {\"descriptor\": ..}`)** | Carried solver answers unpatched: plan-verbatim. Spellings: `language=<family>` (csharp_script / groovy / github_actions / nsis / gdscript), campaign `<FAMILY_UPPER>-<8hex>`, url host `<family>-<10hex>.example.invalid`, file_path `/tmp/huntress-<family>/.<16hex>.stage`, attack T1059 parent / T1105 / none, host_profile `standalone`. Host syntax (pipeline, triggers, Section, `extends`) is inert noise. Don't YAML-parse (PyYAML turns `on:` into `True`). |\n131\t| `.jsp` (D24): line-1 `<%-- HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<TAG>-.. --%>`, `<%@ page contentType=\"text/plain\" %>`, `<%! private static final String DESCRIPTOR_<8HEX> = \"..\";`, `<%= \"inert-analysis-fixture\" %>` | Carried solver, unpatched: plan-verbatim (`language=jsp`, campaign `JSP-<8hex>`, host `jsp-<10hex>.example.invalid`, `/tmp/huntress-jsp/`). Host file `host-jsp-webshell-jsp.jsp` = same shape + `<%-- Modeled request surface only --%>`, host_profile `jsp_webshell`, role staged_chain with downloader-like steps (copy role=). No request/exec code shipped. |\n132\t| `.exs` (D25): line-1 `# HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<TAG>-..`, `descriptor_<8hex> = \"..\"`, `_plan_<8hex> = %{descriptor: descriptor_<8hex>}`; host adds `defmodule Huntress.InertController<8hex> do def show(_conn, _params), do: {:ok, \"inert-analysis-fixture\"} end` | Carried solver, unpatched: plan-verbatim (`language=elixir`, campaign `ELIXIR-<8hex>`, host `elixir-<10hex>.example.invalid`, `/tmp/huntress-elixir/`). Host `host-elixir-phoenix-elixir.exs` = host_profile `elixir_phoenix`, role staged_chain. The Phoenix controller is an inert stub (no `System.cmd`, no `conn` use). |\n133\t| `<%@ Language=VBScript %>` + `<% ' HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:..` in a `.vbs` (D20) | v=3 host for an OLD language (`language=vbscript`, host_profile `classic_asp`). Route by the marker. |\n134\t| Prompt about fetch targets vs network evidence (D17) / process tree (D18) / \"level that doesn't belong\" (D23) / \"order of requests and stages, inert fixture vs real execution primitives\" (D24) / \"follow every transformation, find the setting that didn't survive\" (D25) | Flavour unless a question or an evidence file asks. Network: `lib.codec.network_indicators`/`reconcile`; process: `process_events`/`reconcile_processes`; outlier: `lib.codec.plan_canonical`. |\n135\t| An id whose field suffix is a plan key never asked before | `lib.codec.plan_answer(answer_id, plan, q)` / `plan_key_for` (longest suffix, hyphen->underscore). |\n136\t| `Codec_` key like `ba` / `0a` / `ec` | A hex byte. Transforms are ENCODE-side names: `subtract_modulo_256` decodes by ADDING; `rolling_xor` = c ^ previous CIPHER byte. |\n137\t\n138\t## Codec table (`Codec_<id>='<rep>|<transform>|<key>'`, batch `rem HUNTRESS-CODEC:<rep>|<transform>`; seen D3-D23)\n139\t`lib.codec.find_codecs(text)` / `lib.codec.decode(material, rep, transform, key)` (unknown names -> None => decode by shape).\n140\tReps: base64 (literal/chunks/urlsafe/reversed), hex (pairs/compact/colon/dash/`\\x`/`0x`/buffer/array), percent_hex,\n141\tescaped_octets, unicode_escapes, decimal lists/json_numbers/integer_list/tuple, octal_space, reversed_text/_hex/_decimal/\n142\t_integer_list, plain/split_fragments, v=3 hex_base64, D23 LYR stacks. Transforms (key hex; multi-byte = COMMA list): identity\n143\t(also EMPTY), reverse(_bytes), single_byte_xor, repeating_key_xor, reverse_then_xor, rolling_xor, add_modulo_256 (decode\n144\tSUBTRACTS), subtract_modulo_256 (decode ADDS); batch names carry the parameter (xor_5a, add_7); bash `xor_hex|<key>`.\n145\t\n146\t## Day by day\n147\t**D1-D7 (PS -> Node, 469 ids)**: D1 collection ATT&CK cost 5 wrong before `T1555.003`; D2 7 wrong ATT&CK guesses; **D3 ~1 h 45\n148\tmin, ~127 rejected probes** on batch labels -> NAMING LAWS; D4 VBS control 4 wrong; D5-D6 0 wrong; D7 TT missed 15 ids on new reps.\n149\t**D8-D15 (PHP .. Perl; 615 -> 1026)**: D8 introduced v=3 (copy role/attack/adapter/profiles); each language = 4 polyglots\n150\t(benign_utility/downloader/launcher/staged_chain) + sometimes a `host-<profile>-<lang>`. D14 prompt ATT&CK (T1127.001) was NOT\n151\tthe answer. D15 timed missed ~25 batch-expansion ids -> the label-regime axis.\n152\t**D16-D22 (Ruby, AHK, Apps Script, C#, Groovy, GHA, NSIS; 1095 -> 1417)**: carried marker-routed solver each day; twists D18\n153\tSPLIT array (~30 rejected enum probes, CORRECT T+54 s) and D19 escaped nested carrier (guessed value sank a 46-id bulk; T+39\n154\ts). D20-D22 no twist: CORRECT T+13-25 s 0 wrong; TT 5-9 s, Mastery 8.5-18 s first try (D22 first 6-set Mastery).\n155\t**D23 Press Start to Decode (base `game-resource-loader`; 1461 ids = +44)**: +4 `polyglot-gdscript-*.gd` (line-1 `#` marker,\n156\ttyped `const DESCRIPTOR_<8HEX>: String`). Single: carried solver CORRECT T+52 s, 0 wrong. The twist was the TIMED contract\n157\treshape (hashed members, per-file ids, composite fields, `LYR-` tags, re-rolled vocab, cross-file `handoff-id`): carried\n158\tsolver 593/1495 -> `PF_ID`/`pf_value` + LYR peel -> TT CORRECT T+14 min 16 s (4 batch `-style` ids `..|percent` rejected ->\n159\tcall_double); Mastery (7 sets) lost 12 `-style` + 6 handoff-id (set1 value reused) -> per-set lookup -> CORRECT T+11 min 9 s.\n160\t**D24 Web of Lies (base `jsp-webshell-source`; 1516 ids = +55)**: +4 `polyglot-jsp-*.jsp` + `host-jsp-webshell-jsp.jsp`\n161\t(host_profile `jsp_webshell`): `<%-- HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<TAG>-.. --%>` + `<%! private static final String DESCRIPTOR_<8HEX> =\n162\t\"..\";` + `<%= \"inert-analysis-fixture\" %>`; no request/exec code, so the \"requests vs execution primitives\" prompt was flavour.\n163\tCarried D23 solver unpatched: single CORRECT T+31 s, TT 1560 + Mastery 8 sets first try, 0 generalize workers.\n164\t**D25 Ashes to Assets (base `phoenix-stage-chain`; 1571 ids = +55, 167 members)**: +4 `polyglot-elixir-{benign-utility,\n165\tdownloader,launcher,staged-chain}.exs` + 1 `host-elixir-phoenix-elixir.exs` (11 ids each: role, attack, adapter, campaign,\n166\turl|file-path, stage-count, steps, host-profile, obfuscation, stage-profile, next-language). Artifact: 3-line Elixir scripts --\n167\t`# HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<B64|HEX|HB64|FRAG>-<data>`, `descriptor_<8hex> = \"<same data>\"`, `_plan_<8hex> = %{descriptor:\n168\tdescriptor_<8hex>}`; the host adds an inert Phoenix-style controller module (`def show(_conn, _params), do: {:ok,\n169\t\"inert-analysis-fixture\"}`). Plans: `language=elixir`, campaign `ELIXIR-<8hex>`, url `https://elixir-<10hex>.example.invalid/\n170\tstage`, file_path `/tmp/huntress-elixir/.<16hex>.stage`, attack none/T1105/T1059, host_profile `standalone` vs `elixir_phoenix`;\n171\trole again independent of steps (benign_utility carried `acquire_remote>dispatch_process`; staged_chain carried\n172\t`decode_configuration>return_configuration`) -- copy role=. The prompt's \"configuration changes shape ... reconcile with earlier\n173\tcampaign artifacts ... the setting that didn't survive the rebirth\" was flavour (12th narrative never asked; no config.exs /\n174\truntime.exs / sys.config shipped). Insight: none needed -- the byte-identical D23/D24 solver read the `#` marker unpatched.\n175\tCommands: none beyond the race harness (reuse race of the carried `solve.py` -> `hctf submit --from-solver`). **Single CORRECT\n176\tT+14 s (race win, 0 wrong, one submit)**; TT b59af3dd 1625/1625 first try (solve 1.4 s, total 2.3 s); Mastery 9fd70fc3 (9 sets,\n177\t14625) first try (solve 7.8 s, total 10.4 s). No VARIANT AXIS lines, no generalize workers.\n178\t\n179\t## GM answer conventions learned\n180\t- **Check `answer_format.kind` first.** `enum` lists values (scenario, role). `mitre_attack_id` takes `T####[.###]` or literal\n181\t  `none` (benign_utility). `integer`/`ordered_tokens` (d6+; steps joined with `>`). `exact_text` = plan value or synthetic label.\n182\t  **D23 composite exact_text** = labels joined by `|` with NO spaces, in the order the question lists.\n183\t- **Plan-verbatim fields** (copy exactly): adapter (COM ProgIDs `MSXML2.ServerXMLHTTP.6.0`, LOLBins `CertReq.exe`/`curl.exe`,\n184\t  batch `call`/`set`/`for`, v=3 local_parser/runtime_loader/file_writer/http_client/process_builder/schedule_builder/\n185\t  operation_graph); indicators (campaign_id, host_id, url, file_path, upload_url, next_stage, extension, note_name, handoff_id,\n186\t  cron_path, schedule_path, service_name -- \"exact X indicator\", X = plan key); batch `graph` (linear/single/diamond/fan_out/\n187\t  fallback_retry/cross_language/same_language); Python syntax/obfuscation/carrier/windows_chain; Bash feature/primitive; v=3\n188\t  host_profile (standalone, wsf_jscript, wsf_mixed, hta_jscript, php_webshell, sct_scriptlet, lua_openresty, perl_cgi,\n189\t  ruby_rack, google_docs_sidebar, aspx_inline_csharp, jenkins_pipeline, classic_asp, jsp_webshell (D24), elixir_phoenix (D25);\n190\t  polyglots `standalone`),\n191\t  obfuscation (single: base64/plain_hex/hex_base64/fragmented_hex; timed D23: LYR layer string), stage_profile (single:\n192\t  single_descriptor/two_stage_download_execute/three_stage_decode_write_launch/cross_language_handoff; timed D23 `<colour>_\n193\t  <shape>`), next_language. **Derived D23 fields**: campaign-token (after FIRST hyphen), url-host (hostname, underscores kept),\n194\t  path-leaf (last `/` or `\\` segment, leading dot kept), indicator (first present in the stated order).\n195\t- **v=3 role and attack too.** GM accepts the plan's PARENT ids `T1059` (launcher, staged_chain, hosts) and `T1053`\n196\t  (persistence_descriptor) for every v=3 language through D25 Elixir. The attack question TEXT states the precedence (\"parent\n197\t  technique also accepted ...; for a staged chain or relay the earlier ingress-transfer technique is also accepted; none for a\n198\t  relay\") -- read it before probing. **v=3 role does NOT follow `steps`** (D14-D25) -- copy role=, steps=, stage_profile=.\n199\t- **Role from `steps`** (v=1/v=2 only): decode_configuration,return_configuration = benign_utility; acquire_remote +\n200\t  dispatch_memory/pipe = stager; acquire_remote,write_file = downloader; decode_embedded,write_file = dropper; locate_local,\n201\t  dispatch_process = launcher; read_file/upload,transmit_remote = uploader; transform + recovery_note = impact;\n202\t  build_schedule,register_descriptor = persistence_descriptor; recognize_syntax,reconstruct_intent + `feature=` = advanced_syntax;\n203\t  ends in handoff_script or profile_host..dispatch_process = staged_chain; dispatch_next_stage (Python) = relay.\n204\t- **Role -> ATT&CK** (v=1/v=2; `lib.scripts.role_attack(role, lang)`): benign `none`; downloader/stager T1105; dropper T1140;\n205\t  uploader T1041; impact T1486; persistence_descriptor T1053.003; advanced_syntax T1059.004; launcher/staged_chain/relay = host\n206\t  language T1059.003 batch / .004 bash / .005 VBS / .006 python / .007 JScript and Node. PS scenarios: resource_hijacking T1496,\n207\t  synthetic_collection T1555.003, synthetic_impact T1486. REJECTED: T1218.010, T1620, T1027.009, T1005, T1560, T1119, T1074.\n208\t- **Batch expansion** (enum percent/delayed/call_double/for_indirect): statement regime = Variant axes (default from D16), and\n209\t  the D23 `-style` triple's call_double rule. Fragment JOINER pitfall: `set \"item9=%item0%%item1%..\"` is the JOIN, not fragment\n210\t  9. REJECTED spellings: percent_expansion, immediate, call-double, double_call.\n211\t- **Batch control**: direct, errorlevel_guard (`ver >nul` + `if errorlevel 1 exit /b 1`), goto_dispatch, call_subroutine,\n212\t  if_guard (`if defined X`); separators and `:HUNTRESS_UNUSED` dead labels are NOT control.\n213\t- **VBS control**: direct, select_case, do_once, while_once, error_guard (`On Error Resume Next`..`Err.Raise`), for_once.\n214\t- **JScript styles**: function-style declaration / anonymous_expression / named_expression; invocation-style direct / call /\n215\t  apply; property-style dot / bracket_literal / mixed.\n216\t- **NAMING LAWS**: conditional/bail-out = `<keyword>_guard`; run-once loop = `<keyword>_once`; control transfer =\n217\t  `<keyword>_<action>`. Spelled-out statements and descriptive synonyms have ALWAYS been rejected.\n218\t\n219\t## Pitfalls that cost time\n220\t- **Trusting the single's contract shape in timed modes** (D23: 593/1495 answered, two ~11-14 min recoveries): before a timed\n221\t  run, compare the id GRAMMAR (not just the count) of the timed contract with the single's; an unknown `<fam>-<6hex>-<field>`\n222\t  shape or a new field suffix means route-by-field work, not decoding work. Composite answers: read the order from the question.\n223\t- **Cross-file lookups across Mastery sets** (D23, 6 ids): the same member stem exists in every set; index per inner zip.\n224\t- **A label fix that lands in only one field/mode** (D23 TT fixed `call_double` for the FrAg pool only; Mastery then lost 12 ids\n225\t  on the same construct over other pools): generalize a label rule over EVERY construct instance, then re-run all cases.\n226\t- **Generalize workers dying on context size** (D23 1.39 M-token prompt): never inline a 1500-id contract or the extracted\n227\t  corpus; point at paths and summarise the id grammar.\n228\t- **Enum-walking when the plan did not decode** (D18 ~30 probes; D19 2 + a poisoned bulk): a planless v=3 file is a CARRIER\n229\t  problem; `lib.codec.v3_plan`, else read the bytes around the marker. A GUESSED value in a bulk POST rejects the whole bulk.\n230\t- **Regime keyed on the wrong contract field** (D15-D16, D23): tabulate (construct, GM label) against every contract key AND\n231\t  the asking field at once.\n232\t- **Probing synonyms instead of deriving.** D3 lost ~1.5 h; apply the naming laws first; `hctf labels` seeds candidates.\n233\t- **Generic ATT&CK guesses** (d1, d2): use the role->ATT&CK table; a v=3 `attack=` is authoritative; a prompt's hint is not.\n234\t- **Routing by file extension or name** (D8-D9 `.js` held HTA/WSF/SCT; D19 `.csx` an ASPX page; D20 `.vbs` classic ASP; D23\n235\t  timed members are bare `<6hex>.<ext>`): route by the plan marker, role from the plan.\n236\t- **Answer-id field parsing** (D8): family names contain hyphens/underscores; longest known `-<field>` suffix (`stage-count`/\n237\t  `stage-profile` before `stage`, `campaign-token` before `campaign`).\n238\t- **GM error body saved as the artifact** (D7 TT): check size + sha256 first; tiny `{\"error\":..}` = re-download, exit non-zero.\n239\t- **Stale notes travel with copied solvers** (D8-D25 `solver/NOTES.md` still opens with the D7 heading): date every VARIANT\n240\t  AXIS line by day + attempt id; diagnose EVERY failed attempt.\n241\t- **cmd parsing**: `%item0%` is a variable, not `%0`+`item`; CRLF/LF mixes and `SeT` casing occur. **stage_count != len(steps)**.\n242\t- **Timed modes are a transport race**: fork per set, submit all sets in one call (chunks <= 500 answers / 512 KiB); pair\n243\t  same-named Mastery deliveries by sha256; index nested AES zips once, never decrypt script leaves to sniff for PK.\n244\t- **Reading the narrative prompt as the task** (D8, D15-D25): twelve prompts promised comparison/reconciliation/outlier questions\n245\t  that never came. Diff `answer_ids` first; spend time only on ids the carried solver cannot answer.\n246\t- **Never execute fixtures.** Decode from the Codec const / descriptor plus a restricted interpreter; accept a plan only if it\n247\t  parses as `k=v|..` with `steps` (or `feature`).\n248\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fa8ad0f6-a2ad-4491-87fc-ff4325e1a9f3","uuid":"33b21d78-f7c5-45ca-a85e-86472f74eb21","timestamp":"2026-10-26T13:05:06.593Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/testpwn/.claude/projects/-home-testpwn-huntress-2026/fa8ad0f6-a2ad-4491-87fc-ff4325e1a9f3/tool-results/btjy3t6wc.txt","content":"# script-analysis — technique log (days 1-25; updated after every day)\n\nHow this lane has looked so far (these are observations, not guarantees):\n- **Timed variants MUTATE** (organizer, Day 8: \"new, dynamic variations/mutations ... new unseen effects\"): nothing below is a\n  guarantee for Time Trial / Mastery -- solvers derive structure and degrade per field. **D23 proved it hard: the timed\n  contract had a DIFFERENT SHAPE from the single** (hashed member names, per-file ids, composite fields, `LYR-` carrier tags;\n  see Variant axes) -- the carried solver answered only 593/1495 TT ids.\n- One AES zip `evidence.zip` (password `infected`) of inert \"Huntress Script Triage\" fixtures. **The single contract is\n  CUMULATIVE**: each day keeps every earlier file/question and adds one language; bytes and values re-roll daily. PS (d1, 15\n  ids) -> +JScript (d2, 87) -> +Batch (d3) -> +VBScript (d4) -> +Python (d5, 357) -> +Bash (d6) -> +Node `.mjs` + Bash advanced\n  (d7, 469) -> +PHP + WSF/HTA/webshell hosts (d8, 615) -> +Lua/SCT/OpenResty (d9) -> MOF (d10) -> TypeScript (d11) -> AutoIt\n  (d12) -> AppleScript (d13) -> MSBuild `.proj` (d14, 971) -> Perl + perl_cgi (d15) -> Ruby + ruby_rack (d16, 1095) ->\n  AutoHotkey (d17) -> Apps Script + google_docs_sidebar (d18) -> C# `.csx` + ASPX (d19, 1249) -> Groovy + jenkins_pipeline +\n  classic_asp + 2 Bash (d20, 1329) -> GitHub Actions `.yml` (d21, 1373) -> NSIS `.nsi` (d22, 1417) -> GDScript `.gd` (d23,\n  1461 = +44, no host) -> JSP `.jsp` (d24, 1516 = +55, 4 polyglots + `host-jsp-webshell-jsp`) -> **Elixir `.exs` (d25, 1571 =\n  +55, 167 members: 4 polyglots + `host-elixir-phoenix-elixir`)**. Bash advanced +2 most days (not d12, d15, d17-d19, d21-d23). Since D8 the\n  TITLE/PROMPT is a pun; the new language shows up only in the member list (D16 \"Same Same, But Different\" -> Ruby; D19 \"Sharp\n  Practice\" -> C#; D20 \"The Butler Did It\" -> Jenkins/Groovy; D21 \"Actions Speak Louder\" -> GHA; D22 \"Next, Next, Finish\" ->\n  NSIS; D23 \"Press Start to Decode\" / base `game-resource-loader` -> Godot GDScript; D24 \"Web of Lies\" / base\n  `jsp-webshell-source` -> JSP; **D25 \"Ashes to Assets\" (phoenix pun) / base `phoenix-stage-chain` -> Elixir + Phoenix host;\n  the prompt NAMED the language for the first time**). Diff contract ids against yesterday's.\n- **Forecast cue (D24, CONFIRMED D25)**: the timed plans' `next_language` pool holds only never-shipped languages; each day's\n  new language leaves it. D23 pool had `jsp` -> D24 shipped JSP; D24 pool had `elixir` -> D25 shipped Elixir and the D25 pool\n  lost exactly `elixir`. Remaining 15 = awk, beanshell, dockerfile, erlang, fish, kotlin, makefile, nim, rust, sed, swift,\n  tcl, terraform_hcl, xslt, zsh (6 days left, so ~9 will never ship). Rebuild it nightly from the auto-* expected.json.\n- From day 2 on, every fixture hides a **self-describing plan**: `v=N|steps=a,b|adapter=..|stage_count=..|campaign_id=..|<indicators>`.\n  It sits behind a codec, usually named in a `Codec_<id>` / `CODEC_<id>` / `rem HUNTRESS-CODEC:` const of the form `rep|transform|key`.\n  Most exact_text answers are plan values copied verbatim. From D8 there is also a **`v=3` plan**: it carries `role=` and `attack=`\n  itself, and sits behind a `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<TAG>-` comment.\n- The hard part is **naming CODE SHAPE**: control-flow, expansion, and function/invocation/property styles. These are GM synthetic\n  labels that are not in the plan. Role and scenario are enums, so read `accepted_values`.\n- Single-solve files are named by behaviour (host-context, memory-stage, embedded-write, remote-write, local-dispatch,\n  staged-handoff, outbound-transfer, impact-plan, relay-handoff); answer-id = `<lang>-<role>-<field>`. **Timed D23: members are\n  `<6hex>.<ext>` and ids `<family>-<6hex>-<field>`** -- no behaviour name anywhere; role comes from the plan only.\n- Narrative prompts (D8 siblings, D15 phantom store, D16 equivalence, D17 network reconcile, D18 process tree, D19 bridge, D20\n  controller/agent, D21 trust boundary, D22 setup-vs-payload, D23 \"the level that doesn't belong\", D24 \"order of requests and stages,\n  inert fixture vs real execution primitives\", D25 \"follow every transformation ... the setting that didn't survive the\n  rebirth\") have NEVER been asked as an outlier/compare question. D23's \"correlate with the corpus\"\n  did surface ONCE as a cross-file id: `python-<6hex>-handoff-id` = the `$HandoffId` the PowerShell precursor passes to that .py.\n- Time Trial windows ~5-17 s when the solver fits. Mastery = `setN.` ids; 2 sets d2-d7/d10-d14, 5 sets d8-d9/d15-d21, 6 sets\n  D22 (8502), 7 sets D23 (10465), 8 sets D24 (12480), **9 sets D25 (14625 = 9 x 1625)** -- +1 set/day since D21 -- in one outer `evidence-01.zip` holding `evidence-01..07.zip`; the set loop is\n  count-agnostic. Same-named deliveries: pair by sha256. Timed questions carry `[assigned-artifact-sha256:<hex>]`. From D15 the\n  timed contracts are the untimed regular pool (`run_for_time:false`, `variant_fresh:true`, no deadline).\n\n## Variant axes (what differs between the single, Time Trial and Mastery variants of the SAME day -- parse every value listed)\nEach miss cost one failed timed attempt + a generalize cycle (D6: 4 cycles; D7: 1; D8-D14: 0; D15: 1; D16-D22: 0). **D23: TT\n5 generalize workers, Mastery 3 -- ~14 min + ~11 min to CORRECT**; D24-D25: 0 (per-file shape persisted, solver fit). Auto cases\nD20-D22 (TT 717b8371/f01e0ff9/c355207f, M 1478867c/2620b793/c8d60ca4), D24 (TT 1c3f64b8, M 2afec5c3) and D25 (TT b59af3dd,\nM 9fd70fc3) are value re-rolls;\nD23 TT b10c4da4 / M e24c070d carry the new shape.\n- **CONTRACT SHAPE (D23 NEW; single vs timed)** -- single: semantic ids `<lang>-<role>-<field>` over behaviour-named members\n  (1461). Timed: members renamed `<6hex>.<ext>`, ids `<family>-<6hex>-<field>` (families `powershell`, `jscript`, `batch`,\n  `vbscript`, `python`, `bash`, `bash-advanced`, `nodejs`, `polyglot-<lang>` incl. `polyglot-javascript/jscript/vbscript` for\n  the hosts). New/changed fields: **composite `style`** = labels joined by `|` (JS `function|invocation|property`; batch\n  `graph|control|expansion`; VBS `representation|transform|control`); python `carrier` = `carrier|windows_chain`, python\n  `obfuscation` = `syntax|obfuscation`; **`indicator`** = FIRST plan indicator present in the question's order (url, upload_url,\n  next_stage, file_path, schedule_path, note/recovery-note name, host_id); **`campaign-token`** = campaign after its first\n  hyphen; **`url-host`** = hostname of the plan url; **`path-leaf`** = last segment of file_path; PS `url`/`secondary`/\n  `tertiary` chosen by scenario (resource: wallet/mutex; collection: staged file/UA; impact: note/extension); python\n  **`handoff-id`** (cross-file, below). Parse rule: match `^(?P<fam>.+?)-(?P<stem>[0-9a-f]{6})-(?P<field>[a-z][a-z0-9-]*)$`,\n  require stem == member stem, route by field name; READ the question text for join order / precedence -- it states both.\n  Diff a timed contract's id SHAPE against the single's before trusting the carried solver (D23 solve.py `PF_ID`/`pf_value`).\n  **D24: same grammar again** (TT 1560 = 1495 + 65); the new language joins as `polyglot-jsp` x 5 members x 13 fields (role,\n  attack, steps, stage-count, stage-profile, obfuscation, next-language, campaign, url, file-path, url-host, path-leaf,\n  campaign-token) -- the single's `host-jsp-webshell-jsp` is NOT a separate family in timed (no host-profile field asked).\n  **D25: unchanged again** (TT 1625 = 1560 + 65): `polyglot-elixir` x 5 members x the same 13 fields; the single's\n  `host-elixir-phoenix-elixir` folds into it the same way. Rule held: a new language = +65 timed ids in one `polyglot-<lang>`.\n- **Plan carrier tag (v=3)** -- D8-D22 `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<TAG>-<data>` with tags `B64`/`HEX`/`HB64`/`FRAG` (= obfuscation\n  profile base64/plain_hex/hex_base64/fragmented_hex), fixed per file in every delivery. D18 `SPLIT` = layout tag (no data;\n  the data is the next multi-line `[..].join(\"\")` array). **D23 timed: `LYR-<l1>_<l2>[_<l3>]-<data>`**, layers from {`b64`,\n  `b32`, `hex`, `rev`, `frag`} in ENCODE order (decode last-first: frag = drop `.`, rev = reverse, b32 = upper+pad); the\n  obfuscation answer is the layer string itself (`hex_hex_hex`, `b64_b32`, `b32_rev`, 54 distinct seen). Apps Script splits the\n  LYR string across an array -> join first, then LYR-peel. The single still used B64/HEX/HB64/FRAG. Parse rule: tag-directed\n  peel when the tag parses as a layer list, else shape peel (max 4 layers); accept only `v=`.\n  D24-D25 timed: same 5 layer names (D25 e.g. `hex_b64_b32`, `hex_b32`); no new layer name in 3 days.\n- **Plan VOCABULARY re-roll (D23-D24 timed)** -- stage_profile `<colour>_<shape>` (amber/cobalt/ivory/onyx/ruby/slate/teal/umber x\n  braid/ladder/lattice/pivot/spindle/weave), next_language anything (awk, beanshell, dockerfile, elixir, erlang, fish, jsp,\n  kotlin, makefile, nim, rust, sed, swift, tcl, terraform_hcl, xslt, zsh; D24 minus jsp; D25 minus elixir), stage_count 2-8, timed polyglot\n  roles span all 8 (persistence_descriptor/T1053, uploader/T1041, dropper/T1140, stager/T1105 included), python syntax/obfuscation new\n  (match_case, walrus_binding, class_staticmethod, marshal_envelope_plan, closure_cells, string_table, lambda_indirection).\n  Parse rule: plan-verbatim; never validate plan values against a known list.\n- **GM label regime (batch `expansion`)** -- SAME bytes, DIFFERENT label by key. Old regime (D3-D14 + D15 single): whole\n  handoff, `echo(!var!)` => delayed unless a FOR/h-pool rule fires. Statement regime (D15 timed, D16+ every mode; `run_for_time\n  is False` OR `started_at >= 2026-10-16`; `lib.codec.label_regime`): label the JOIN STATEMENT -- `!a!!b!` = delayed; `for ..\n  do call set` = for_indirect; bare `call set \"x=%%h0%%..\"` = call_double; `call set` over other pools = percent; plain `set\n  \"x=%a%%b%\"` = percent. **D23 FIELD-keyed: inside the composite `-style` triple a `call set \"..%%x%%..\"` second pass is\n  `call_double` on ANY pool** (TT b10c4da4 4 ids, Mastery e24c070d 12 ids rejected as `percent`), while the stand-alone\n  `-expansion` field keeps `percent` for the same construct. When byte-identical constructs get different labels, tabulate\n  (construct, label) against EVERY contract key (started_at, run_for_time, variant_fresh) AND the asking field at once.\n- **Mastery set scoping (D23)** -- the same member stem (`4c1097.py`) recurs in all 7 sets with a different precursor value per\n  set; a cross-file lookup indexed over the whole bundle returned set1's handoff id for sets 2-7 (6 rejected). Parse rule: index\n  and resolve cross-file references PER SET (inner `evidence-0N.zip`), never per outer artifact. D24-D25: stems again identical\n  across all sets (`588efb.jsp`, `a7470f.exs` in set1..set9) with set-distinct plans.\n- **Codec per file** -- rep x transform x key re-roll per variant; NEW rep names appear only on variants (D7 TT\n  `unicode_escapes`, `json_numbers`, `reversed_base64`, Bash `xor_hex|cd`). Decode by material SHAPE x named transform; accept\n  only `v=`. Spec arity: `rep|transform|key`, `rep|` (empty = identity), or transform folded into the rep (`xor_hex|cd`).\n- **Plan carrier NESTING (D10 MOF, D19 ASPX)** -- inner script as an escaped string of the host; unescape (`\\n \\\" \\\\`, `\"\"`,\n  `&quot;`/CDATA, `\"`) and rescan; call `lib.codec.v3_plan` before anything else.\n- **Plan carrier host syntax (v=3)** -- marker in the host's comment: `//`, `--`, `;`, `<!-- -->`, `#` (Perl, Ruby, YAML,\n  **GDScript**), `'` in `<% %>`. Descriptor forms: `$descriptor_<id>`, `var/local/const/final String/my descriptor_<id> =`,\n  AutoIt `Global Const`, AppleScript `property ..:`, AHK `:=`, Ruby `DESCRIPTOR_<8HEX> =`, `<HuntressDescriptor>`, ASP `Dim`\n  then assign, builder maps, YAML `env: HUNTRESS_DESCRIPTOR:` (no id), NSIS `StrCpy $0 \"..\"` (no name), **GDScript typed const\n  `const DESCRIPTOR_<8HEX>: String = \"..\"`** (type annotation between name and `=`). Parse rule: regex the MARKER\n  `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V\\d+\\s*:\\s*(\\w*)-?\\s*([^\\s\"'<>\\]]+)` over raw bytes; never anchor on `=`/`:=`/`set`/`<-`.\n  D25 Elixir: `#` marker + a plain lowercase binding `descriptor_<8hex> = \"..\"` (NOT the forecast `@descriptor` attribute or a\n  `~s()` sigil) + `_plan_<8hex> = %{descriptor: ..}` map.\n- **Literal shapes (D6-D7)** -- radix from the code; base64 std AND urlsafe; reverse the LIST vs the TEXT (try both); join\n  split chunks / `+=` / adjacent strings / `.`-FRAG / `[..].join(\"\")` first; carriers may be frozen exes (D6 cx_Freeze).\n- **Transport/runner, not variant** -- D7 TT `{\"error\":\"rate_limited\"}` saved as the zip; D8 TT 503; D16 60 s runner cap; D23\n  one TT generalize worker died \"Prompt is too long\" (1.39 M tokens: the 1495-id contract + artifacts inlined). Never harvest\n  these as cases.\n\n## Recognition cues -> first move\n| You see | First move |\n|---|---|\n| `evidence.zip`, \"method=AES Encrypted\" | Triage already extracted it (`work/extracted/`) and decoded every plan. Diff the member list / contract ids against yesterday's to find the new language. Open members with `lib.common.read_member` (zipfile can't read AES). |\n| Prior-day languages in the contract | Cumulative: rerun the carried marker-routed solver FIRST (D9-D23 single: it covered each new v=3 language unchanged except D18/D19 carrier patches). Any planless file: `lib.codec.v3_plan(text)`. Spend thinking on the new language and on label regimes. |\n| **Timed contract ids `<family>-<6hex>-<field>`, members `<6hex>.<ext>` (D23)** | Contract-shape change, not a decode failure. Count ids answered vs asked FIRST; route by `PF_ID` + field name; composite fields join with `\\|` in the question's order; indicator by the question's precedence list; resolve cross-file ids (`handoff-id`) per set. |\n| `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:LYR-<l>_<l>-..` (D23 timed) | Tag = encode layers (b64/b32/hex/rev/frag); undo last-first; obfuscation answer = the layer string verbatim. |\n| `.ps1` `$encodedMaterial = [Convert]::FromBase64String('..')` + `$nativeTypes` | `base64 -d` -> JSON descriptor: url/wallet/mutex/UA/file/ext/note by SHAPE. `$nativeTypes`: Process/Registry+wallet=resource, ZipFile/HttpWebRequest=collection, Aes/DirectoryInfo=impact. `invoke-python-stage.ps1` carries `$HandoffId = 'PSPY-<16HEX>'` + `$NextStage`. |\n| `.js` WSH, `decode_*`/`recover_*`/`inspect_*`, XOR key arrays | Run each file in an empty `node` `vm` (no require/ActiveXObject, `eval` -> capture); keep the first object with `steps`. Styles from the `inspect_*` body. |\n| `.bat/.cmd` `rem HUNTRESS-CODEC:` / `set \"itemN=..` / `:HUNTRESS_INSPECT` | Plan in `set` fragments; emulate cmd expansion in Python. Expansion label: statement regime, but `call set %%x%%` inside a `-style` triple = call_double (Variant axes). Never run cmd. |\n| `.vbs` `Const Material_<id>`, `Const Codec_<id> = \"rep|transform|key\"` | Decode from the Codec const; rep/transform = Codec fields 1/2 verbatim. Control = construct wrapping `Decode_` inside `Recover_`. |\n| `.py` `*-recovered.py` with `MATERIAL_<id>`, `CODEC_<id>` | Decode from CODEC (or AST-whitelisted `decode_(load_(..))`). Plan v=2 carries syntax/obfuscation/carrier/windows_chain verbatim. |\n| `.sh` `readonly Material_<id>` + `readonly Codec_<id>` (+ `Feature_<id>()`) | Decode from the Codec const (multi-byte key = COMMA list). `Feature_` fixtures: role `advanced_syntax`, feature/primitive/campaign/stage_count/steps plan-verbatim, T1059.004. Never run bash. |\n| `.mjs` ESM `const Material_<id>`, async `load_/decode_/recover_/inspect_/plan_<id>` | Static decode (`lib.codec.find_codecs` + shape fallback). Plan fields verbatim. |\n| `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<TAG>-..` in any comment + a descriptor literal (`.php .lua .js .vbs .mof .ts .au3 .applescript .proj .pl .rb .ahk .gs .csx .groovy .yml .nsi .gd`) | **Route by the marker before the extension.** Peel to `v=3|language=..|role=..|attack=..|adapter=..|host_profile=..|obfuscation_profile=..|stage_profile=..|next_language=..|stage_count=..|steps=..|campaign_id=..|url=..|file_path=..`. EVERY answer incl. role/attack is plan-verbatim. |\n| `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:SPLIT` (no data) + `const HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1_SPLIT_<id> = [..].join(\"\")` (D18) | Join the array literals, drop the `<TAG>-` head, peel. 44 new ids unanswered = CARRIER bug; never walk the role enum. |\n| ASPX `<script runat=\"server\">` + `EmbeddedCsx_<id> = \"// HUNTRESS..\\n..\\\"..\\\";\"` (D19) | NESTED carrier: unescape `\\n`/`\\\"`/`\\\\` (and `\"\"`, `&quot;`, CDATA) and rescan; `lib.codec.v3_plan` does. |\n| New language, plain one-line marker: `.csx` (D19), `.groovy` (D20), `.yml` (D21 `env: HUNTRESS_DESCRIPTOR`), `.nsi` (D22 `StrCpy $0`), `.exs` (D25, next row), **`.gd` (D23: line-1 `# HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<TAG>-..`, `extends RefCounted`, `const DESCRIPTOR_<8HEX>: String = \"..\"`, `func build_plan_<id>() -> Dictionary: return {\"descriptor\": ..}`)** | Carried solver answers unpatched: plan-verbatim. Spellings: `language=<family>` (csharp_script / groovy / github_actions / nsis / gdscript), campaign `<FAMILY_UPPER>-<8hex>`, url host `<family>-<10hex>.example.invalid`, file_path `/tmp/huntress-<family>/.<16hex>.stage`, attack T1059 parent / T1105 / none, host_profile `standalone`. Host syntax (pipeline, triggers, Section, `extends`) is inert noise. Don't YAML-parse (PyYAML turns `on:` into `True`). |\n| `.jsp` (D24): line-1 `<%-- HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<TAG>-.. --%>`, `<%@ page contentType=\"text/plain\" %>`, `<%! private static final String DESCRIPTOR_<8HEX> = \"..\";`, `<%= \"inert-analysis-fixture\" %>` | Carried solver, unpatched: plan-verbatim (`language=jsp`, campaign `JSP-<8hex>`, host `jsp-<10hex>.example.invalid`, `/tmp/huntress-jsp/`). Host file `host-jsp-webshell-jsp.jsp` = same shape + `<%-- Modeled request surface only --%>`, host_profile `jsp_webshell`, role staged_chain with downloader-like steps (copy role=). No request/exec code shipped. |\n| `.exs` (D25): line-1 `# HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<TAG>-..`, `descriptor_<8hex> = \"..\"`, `_plan_<8hex> = %{descriptor: descriptor_<8hex>}`; host adds `defmodule Huntress.InertController<8hex> do def show(_conn, _params), do: {:ok, \"inert-analysis-fixture\"} end` | Carried solver, unpatched: plan-verbatim (`language=elixir`, campaign `ELIXIR-<8hex>`, host `elixir-<10hex>.example.invalid`, `/tmp/huntress-elixir/`). Host `host-elixir-phoenix-elixir.exs` = host_profile `elixir_phoenix`, role staged_chain. The Phoenix controller is an inert stub (no `System.cmd`, no `conn` use). |\n| `<%@ Language=VBScript %>` + `<% ' HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:..` in a `.vbs` (D20) | v=3 host for an OLD language (`language=vbscript`, host_profile `classic_asp`). Route by the marker. |\n| Prompt about fetch targets vs network evidence (D17) / process tree (D18) / \"level that doesn't belong\" (D23) / \"order of requests and stages, inert fixture vs real execution primitives\" (D24) / \"follow every transformation, find the setting that didn't survive\" (D25) | Flavour unless a question or an evidence file asks. Network: `lib.codec.network_indicators`/`reconcile`; process: `process_events`/`reconcile_processes`; outlier: `lib.codec.plan_canonical`. |\n| An id whose field suffix is a plan key never asked before | `lib.codec.plan_answer(answer_id, plan, q)` / `plan_key_for` (longest suffix, hyphen->underscore). |\n| `Codec_` key like `ba` / `0a` / `ec` | A hex byte. Transforms are ENCODE-side names: `subtract_modulo_256` decodes by ADDING; `rolling_xor` = c ^ previous CIPHER byte. |\n\n## Codec table (`Codec_<id>='<rep>|<transform>|<key>'`, batch `rem HUNTRESS-CODEC:<rep>|<transform>`; seen D3-D23)\n`lib.codec.find_codecs(text)` / `lib.codec.decode(material, rep, transform, key)` (unknown names -> None => decode by shape).\nReps: base64 (literal/chunks/urlsafe/reversed), hex (pairs/compact/colon/dash/`\\x`/`0x`/buffer/array), percent_hex,\nescaped_octets, unicode_escapes, decimal lists/json_numbers/integer_list/tuple, octal_space, reversed_text/_hex/_decimal/\n_integer_list, plain/split_fragments, v=3 hex_base64, D23 LYR stacks. Transforms (key hex; multi-byte = COMMA list): identity\n(also EMPTY), reverse(_bytes), single_byte_xor, repeating_key_xor, reverse_then_xor, rolling_xor, add_modulo_256 (decode\nSUBTRACTS), subtract_modulo_256 (decode ADDS); batch names carry the parameter (xor_5a, add_7); bash `xor_hex|<key>`.\n\n## Day by day\n**D1-D7 (PS -> Node, 469 ids)**: D1 collection ATT&CK cost 5 wrong before `T1555.003`; D2 7 wrong ATT&CK guesses; **D3 ~1 h 45\nmin, ~127 rejected probes** on batch labels -> NAMING LAWS; D4 VBS control 4 wrong; D5-D6 0 wrong; D7 TT missed 15 ids on new reps.\n**D8-D15 (PHP .. Perl; 615 -> 1026)**: D8 introduced v=3 (copy role/attack/adapter/profiles); each language = 4 polyglots\n(benign_utility/downloader/launcher/staged_chain) + sometimes a `host-<profile>-<lang>`. D14 prompt ATT&CK (T1127.001) was NOT\nthe answer. D15 timed missed ~25 batch-expansion ids -> the label-regime axis.\n**D16-D22 (Ruby, AHK, Apps Script, C#, Groovy, GHA, NSIS; 1095 -> 1417)**: carried marker-routed solver each day; twists D18\nSPLIT array (~30 rejected enum probes, CORRECT T+54 s) and D19 escaped nested carrier (guessed value sank a 46-id bulk; T+39\ns). D20-D22 no twist: CORRECT T+13-25 s 0 wrong; TT 5-9 s, Mastery 8.5-18 s first try (D22 first 6-set Mastery).\n**D23 Press Start to Decode (base `game-resource-loader`; 1461 ids = +44)**: +4 `polyglot-gdscript-*.gd` (line-1 `#` marker,\ntyped `const DESCRIPTOR_<8HEX>: String`). Single: carried solver CORRECT T+52 s, 0 wrong. The twist was the TIMED contract\nreshape (hashed members, per-file ids, composite fields, `LYR-` tags, re-rolled vocab, cross-file `handoff-id`): carried\nsolver 593/1495 -> `PF_ID`/`pf_value` + LYR peel -> TT CORRECT T+14 min 16 s (4 batch `-style` ids `..|percent` rejected ->\ncall_double); Mastery (7 sets) lost 12 `-style` + 6 handoff-id (set1 value reused) -> per-set lookup -> CORRECT T+11 min 9 s.\n**D24 Web of Lies (base `jsp-webshell-source`; 1516 ids = +55)**: +4 `polyglot-jsp-*.jsp` + `host-jsp-webshell-jsp.jsp`\n(host_profile `jsp_webshell`): `<%-- HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<TAG>-.. --%>` + `<%! private static final String DESCRIPTOR_<8HEX> =\n\"..\";` + `<%= \"inert-analysis-fixture\" %>`; no request/exec code, so the \"requests vs execution primitives\" prompt was flavour.\nCarried D23 solver unpatched: single CORRECT T+31 s, TT 1560 + Mastery 8 sets first try, 0 generalize workers.\n**D25 Ashes to Assets (base `phoenix-stage-chain`; 1571 ids = +55, 167 members)**: +4 `polyglot-elixir-{benign-utility,\ndownloader,launcher,staged-chain}.exs` + 1 `host-elixir-phoenix-elixir.exs` (11 ids each: role, attack, adapter, campaign,\nurl|file-path, stage-count, steps, host-profile, obfuscation, stage-profile, next-language). Artifact: 3-line Elixir scripts --\n`# HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<B64|HEX|HB64|FRAG>-<data>`, `descriptor_<8hex> = \"<same data>\"`, `_plan_<8hex> = %{descriptor:\ndescriptor_<8hex>}`; the host adds an inert Phoenix-style controller module (`def show(_conn, _params), do: {:ok,\n\"inert-analysis-fixture\"}`). Plans: `language=elixir`, campaign `ELIXIR-<8hex>`, url `https://elixir-<10hex>.example.invalid/\nstage`, file_path `/tmp/huntress-elixir/.<16hex>.stage`, attack none/T1105/T1059, host_profile `standalone` vs `elixir_phoenix`;\nrole again independent of steps (benign_utility carried `acquire_remote>dispatch_process`; staged_chain carried\n`decode_configuration>return_configuration`) -- copy role=. The prompt's \"configuration changes shape ... reconcile with earlier\ncampaign artifacts ... the setting that didn't survive the rebirth\" was flavour (12th narrative never asked; no config.exs /\nruntime.exs / sys.config shipped). Insight: none needed -- the byte-identical D23/D24 solver read the `#` marker unpatched.\nCommands: none beyond the race harness (reuse race of the carried `solve.py` -> `hctf submit --from-solver`). **Single CORRECT\nT+14 s (race win, 0 wrong, one submit)**; TT b59af3dd 1625/1625 first try (solve 1.4 s, total 2.3 s); Mastery 9fd70fc3 (9 sets,\n14625) first try (solve 7.8 s, total 10.4 s). No VARIANT AXIS lines, no generalize workers.\n\n## GM answer conventions learned\n- **Check `answer_format.kind` first.** `enum` lists values (scenario, role). `mitre_attack_id` takes `T####[.###]` or literal\n  `none` (benign_utility). `integer`/`ordered_tokens` (d6+; steps joined with `>`). `exact_text` = plan value or synthetic label.\n  **D23 composite exact_text** = labels joined by `|` with NO spaces, in the order the question lists.\n- **Plan-verbatim fields** (copy exactly): adapter (COM ProgIDs `MSXML2.ServerXMLHTTP.6.0`, LOLBins `CertReq.exe`/`curl.exe`,\n  batch `call`/`set`/`for`, v=3 local_parser/runtime_loader/file_writer/http_client/process_builder/schedule_builder/\n  operation_graph); indicators (campaign_id, host_id, url, file_path, upload_url, next_stage, extension, note_name, handoff_id,\n  cron_path, schedule_path, service_name -- \"exact X indicator\", X = plan key); batch `graph` (linear/single/diamond/fan_out/\n  fallback_retry/cross_language/same_language); Python syntax/obfuscation/carrier/windows_chain; Bash feature/primitive; v=3\n  host_profile (standalone, wsf_jscript, wsf_mixed, hta_jscript, php_webshell, sct_scriptlet, lua_openresty, perl_cgi,\n  ruby_rack, google_docs_sidebar, aspx_inline_csharp, jenkins_pipeline, classic_asp, jsp_webshell (D24), elixir_phoenix (D25);\n  polyglots `standalone`),\n  obfuscation (single: base64/plain_hex/hex_base64/fragmented_hex; timed D23: LYR layer string), stage_profile (single:\n  single_descriptor/two_stage_download_execute/three_stage_decode_write_launch/cross_language_handoff; timed D23 `<colour>_\n  <shape>`), next_language. **Derived D23 fields**: campaign-token (after FIRST hyphen), url-host (hostname, underscores kept),\n  path-leaf (last `/` or `\\` segment, leading dot kept), indicator (first present in the stated order).\n- **v=3 role and attack too.** GM accepts the plan's PARENT ids `T1059` (launcher, staged_chain, hosts) and `T1053`\n  (persistence_descriptor) for every v=3 language through D25 Elixir. The attack question TEXT states the precedence (\"parent\n  technique also accepted ...; for a staged chain or relay the earlier ingress-transfer technique is also accepted; none for a\n  relay\") -- read it before probing. **v=3 role does NOT follow `steps`** (D14-D25) -- copy role=, steps=, stage_profile=.\n- **Role from `steps`** (v=1/v=2 only): decode_configuration,return_configuration = benign_utility; acquire_remote +\n  dispatch_memory/pipe = stager; acquire_remote,write_file = downloader; decode_embedded,write_file = dropper; locate_local,\n  dispatch_process = launcher; read_file/upload,transmit_remote = uploader; transform + recovery_note = impact;\n  build_schedule,register_descriptor = persistence_descriptor; recognize_syntax,reconstruct_intent + `feature=` = advanced_syntax;\n  ends in handoff_script or profile_host..dispatch_process = staged_chain; dispatch_next_stage (Python) = relay.\n- **Role -> ATT&CK** (v=1/v=2; `lib.scripts.role_attack(role, lang)`): benign `none`; downloader/stager T1105; dropper T1140;\n  uploader T1041; impact T1486; persistence_descriptor T1053.003; advanced_syntax T1059.004; launcher/staged_chain/relay = host\n  language T1059.003 batch / .004 bash / .005 VBS / .006 python / .007 JScript and Node. PS scenarios: resource_hijacking T1496,\n  synthetic_collection T1555.003, synthetic_impact T1486. REJECTED: T1218.010, T1620, T1027.009, T1005, T1560, T1119, T1074.\n- **Batch expansion** (enum percent/delayed/call_double/for_indirect): statement regime = Variant axes (default from D16), and\n  the D23 `-style` triple's call_double rule. Fragment JOINER pitfall: `set \"item9=%item0%%item1%..\"` is the JOIN, not fragment\n  9. REJECTED spellings: percent_expansion, immediate, call-double, double_call.\n- **Batch control**: direct, errorlevel_guard (`ver >nul` + `if errorlevel 1 exit /b 1`), goto_dispatch, call_subroutine,\n  if_guard (`if defined X`); separators and `:HUNTRESS_UNUSED` dead labels are NOT control.\n- **VBS control**: direct, select_case, do_once, while_once, error_guard (`On Error Resume Next`..`Err.Raise`), for_once.\n- **JScript styles**: function-style declaration / anonymous_expression / named_expression; invocation-style direct / call /\n  apply; property-style dot / bracket_literal / mixed.\n- **NAMING LAWS**: conditional/bail-out = `<keyword>_guard`; run-once loop = `<keyword>_once`; control transfer =\n  `<keyword>_<action>`. Spelled-out statements and descriptive synonyms have ALWAYS been rejected.\n\n## Pitfalls that cost time\n- **Trusting the single's contract shape in timed modes** (D23: 593/1495 answered, two ~11-14 min recoveries): before a timed\n  run, compare the id GRAMMAR (not just the count) of the timed contract with the single's; an unknown `<fam>-<6hex>-<field>`\n  shape or a new field suffix means route-by-field work, not decoding work. Composite answers: read the order from the question.\n- **Cross-file lookups across Mastery sets** (D23, 6 ids): the same member stem exists in every set; index per inner zip.\n- **A label fix that lands in only one field/mode** (D23 TT fixed `call_double` for the FrAg pool only; Mastery then lost 12 ids\n  on the same construct over other pools): generalize a label rule over EVERY construct instance, then re-run all cases.\n- **Generalize workers dying on context size** (D23 1.39 M-token prompt): never inline a 1500-id contract or the extracted\n  corpus; point at paths and summarise the id grammar.\n- **Enum-walking when the plan did not decode** (D18 ~30 probes; D19 2 + a poisoned bulk): a planless v=3 file is a CARRIER\n  problem; `lib.codec.v3_plan`, else read the bytes around the marker. A GUESSED value in a bulk POST rejects the whole bulk.\n- **Regime keyed on the wrong contract field** (D15-D16, D23): tabulate (construct, GM label) against every contract key AND\n  the asking field at once.\n- **Probing synonyms instead of deriving.** D3 lost ~1.5 h; apply the naming laws first; `hctf labels` seeds candidates.\n- **Generic ATT&CK guesses** (d1, d2): use the role->ATT&CK table; a v=3 `attack=` is authoritative; a prompt's hint is not.\n- **Routing by file extension or name** (D8-D9 `.js` held HTA/WSF/SCT; D19 `.csx` an ASPX page; D20 `.vbs` classic ASP; D23\n  timed members are bare `<6hex>.<ext>`): route by the plan marker, role from the plan.\n- **Answer-id field parsing** (D8): family names contain hyphens/underscores; longest known `-<field>` suffix (`stage-count`/\n  `stage-profile` before `stage`, `campaign-token` before `campaign`).\n- **GM error body saved as the artifact** (D7 TT): check size + sha256 first; tiny `{\"error\":..}` = re-download, exit non-zero.\n- **Stale notes travel with copied solvers** (D8-D25 `solver/NOTES.md` still opens with the D7 heading): date every VARIANT\n  AXIS line by day + attempt id; diagnose EVERY failed attempt.\n- **cmd parsing**: `%item0%` is a variable, not `%0`+`item`; CRLF/LF mixes and `SeT` casing occur. **stage_count != len(steps)**.\n- **Timed modes are a transport race**: fork per set, submit all sets in one call (chunks <= 500 answers / 512 KiB); pair\n  same-named Mastery deliveries by sha256; index nested AES zips once, never decrypt script leaves to sniff for PK.\n- **Reading the narrative prompt as the task** (D8, D15-D25): twelve prompts promised comparison/reconciliation/outlier questions\n  that never came. Diff `answer_ids` first; spend time only on ids the carried solver cannot answer.\n- **Never execute fixtures.** Decode from the Codec const / descriptor plus a restricted interpreter; accept a plan only if it\n  parses as `k=v|..` with `steps` (or `feature`).\n","numLines":248,"startLine":1,"totalLines":248}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01TPynqn6c8NbnQM8cyiUQMS","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
