{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018e9pAk26orHLvwkUZoseAQ","type":"tool_result","content":"<persisted-output>\nOutput too large (105.1KB). Full output saved to: /home/testpwn/.claude/projects/-home-testpwn-huntress-2026/fa8ad0f6-a2ad-4491-87fc-ff4325e1a9f3/tool-results/b3ckuc7rp.txt\n\nPreview (first 2KB):\n# script-analysis — coverage atlas (D1-D25 seen vs. D26+ candidates)\n\nUpdated 2026-10-25 after D25 (single 1571 ids, 167 members; \"Ashes to Assets\" / base `phoenix-stage-chain` added 4\n`polyglot-elixir-*.exs` + 1 `host-elixir-phoenix-elixir.exs` (host_profile `elixir_phoenix`) -- line-1 `# HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:\n<TAG>-..`, plain binding `descriptor_<8hex> = \"..\"`, `_plan_<8hex> = %{descriptor: ..}`; the host adds an inert Phoenix\ncontroller `def show(_conn, _params), do: {:ok, \"inert-analysis-fixture\"}`). Carried D23 solver (byte-identical since D23)\nanswered everything: single CORRECT T+14 s (race win), TT 1625 ids and Mastery (**9 sets**, 14625 ids) first try; per-file\ntimed grammar + `LYR-` tags unchanged for the 3rd day (elixir joins as `polyglot-elixir`, 5 members x 13 fields). The prompt\n(\"configuration ... changed shape ... reconcile with earlier campaign artifacts ... the setting that didn't survive the\nrebirth\") was never asked -- 12th narrative in a row. **Forecast signal CONFIRMED (2nd data point)**: D24's timed\n`next_language` pool contained elixir and D25 shipped Elixir; D25's pool dropped exactly `elixir`. Remaining 15 (the D26-D31\nroadmap; 6 days left): awk, beanshell, dockerfile, erlang, fish, kotlin, makefile, nim, rust, sed, swift, tcl, terraform_hcl,\nxslt, zsh. Re-check the pool from every auto-* expected.json each night; the language that leaves it is the day's new one.\nD24-night: built per-file-hashed-contract (2nd try), next-lang-pool-polyglot-battery, kotlin-beanshell-literal-route; failed\nonce beam-erlang-elixir-route, zsh-fish-shell-route, jsp-jspx-unicode-carrier (all three: th