{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AeJPEEyVsMkcHYGbgmrjww","type":"tool_result","content":"## Readiness gaps\nBuilt by the nightly prebuild (dropped from the queue, still usable from lib/): D16-D23 nights (see git history) and D24 night\nper-file-hashed-contract, next-lang-pool-polyglot-battery, kotlin-beanshell-literal-route. Given up (2 attempts):\npython-exec-onion-static, evidence-type-router, file-registry-telemetry-reconcile, build-manifest-hooks,\nmacos-pkg-installer-scripts. Prebuild gate: lib imports limited to hctf/prebuild.py ALLOWED_IMPORTS (stdlib parsers +\nCrypto/cryptography/dpkt/Evtx/pefile/olefile/dnfile; REJECTED so far: csv, ast, shlex, marshal, pathlib, pickletools,\n`__import__()` calls -- use os.path and hand-rolled parsers) and the lane fixture test's 2 s find_codecs budget (failed 4\nprebuilds -> find-codecs-speed-gate goes FIRST). Priority-1 order for D26: the speed gate, then the pool languages most\nlikely next (Erlang = BEAM sibling of D25 Elixir; zsh/fish shell twins; Rust), then the remaining pool languages (awk/sed,\nnim/swift/tcl, terraform_hcl; kotlin/beanshell, dockerfile/makefile and xslt already have built routes), then the\nnarrative-model gaps (config survival D25, webshell requests D24) and leftovers.\n\n```json\n[\n  {\"id\": \"find-codecs-speed-gate\", \"concept\": \"make lib.codec.find_codecs fast (lazy regex compile + cheap substring gates) so carrier prebuilds stop failing the 2 s fixture budget\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D24 night: 3 of 6 script-lane prebuilds (beam, zsh-fish, jsp-jspx) failed ONLY on tests/test_lane_fixtures.py find_codecs > 2 s (nested_msbuild_entities.json 2.18-2.66 s\n  {\"id\": \"beam-erlang-elixir-route\", \"concept\": \"Erlang `.erl`/escript carriers (first `%` comment marker) + Elixir twists beyond the D25 shape\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Elixir SHIPPED D25 in the simplest form (`# ` marker, `descriptor_<8hex> = \\\"..\\\"`, `%{descriptor: ..}` map, inert Phoenix controller) and the carried solver read it unpatched; Erlang (BEAM sibling) is stil\n  {\"id\": \"zsh-fish-shell-route\", \"concept\": \"zsh and fish shell carriers (and a possible `zsh-advanced`/`fish-advanced` Feature_ set like bash-advanced)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"zsh: `typeset -r DESCRIPTOR_X=\\\"..\\\"`, `readonly`, parameter-expansion flags `${(j::)arr}` (join), `${(s:,:)x}` (split), `${(Oa)arr}` (reverse array), `${(%)..}`, `print -r --`, `$'..'` ANSI-C, `zm\n  {\"id\": \"rust-cargo-buildrs-route\", \"concept\": \"Rust carriers: `.rs` scripts, `build.rs` build-time execution, Cargo manifests\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"rust is in the D25 next_language pool (15 left) and the lane has had no compiled-language source day since C# (D19). Shapes: `// HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:..` or `//!`/`/* */` doc comments, `const DESCRIPTOR_X: &str = \\\"..\\\";`,\n  {\"id\": \"awk-sed-program-route\", \"concept\": \"awk and sed programs as carriers (string juxtaposition, sprintf char codes, sed `y///` transliteration and `s///e`)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"awk: `#!/usr/bin/awk -f`, `BEGIN { descriptor_x = \\\"..\\\" }`, concatenation by JUXTAPOSITION (`\\\"ab\\\" \\\"cd\\\"` or `a b`), `sprintf(\\\"%c\\\", n)` char-code loops, `split()`+loop joins, `-v x=..\n  {\"id\": \"nim-swift-tcl-literal-route\", \"concept\": \"Nim, Swift and Tcl string-literal forms that can hide the descriptor\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"All in the pool. Nim: `# ` / `#[ ]#` comments, `const descriptorX = \\\"..\\\"`, `let`, raw `r\\\"..\\\"`, `\\\"\\\"\\\"..\\\"\\\"\\\"`, `&` concat, `\\\\x41` escapes, `import osproc` + `execProcess`/`startProcess`. Swift: `#!/usr/bin/swift`, `//` + `\n  {\"id\": \"terraform-hcl-function-fold\", \"concept\": \"Terraform HCL literal folds: heredocs, interpolation, `join`/`base64decode`/`format` calls\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"terraform_hcl in the pool (family name would be `polyglot-terraform_hcl`, campaign `TERRAFORM_HCL-<8hex>`, url host `terraform_hcl-<10hex>.example.invalid` -- underscores kept like github_actions D21). cloud\n  {\"id\": \"stage-config-survival-diff\", \"concept\": \"config that changes shape across a stage chain and the key that 'didn't survive' (D25 prompt; never asked yet)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D25 prompt: 'Configuration starts out in Elixir source and has changed shape by the time an inert Phoenix-hosted stage picks it up. Follow every transformation, reconcile each one with ear\n  {\"id\": \"composite-label-field-regime\", \"concept\": \"synthetic labels keyed by the asking FIELD (composite `-style` triple vs stand-alone field)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D23: batch `call set \\\"..%%x%%..\\\"` = call_double inside `graph|control|expansion` (TT 4 + Mastery 12 ids rejected as percent) but percent in the stand-alone `-expansion` field. Extend lib.codec.label_expa\n  {\"id\": \"jsp-jspx-unicode-carrier\", \"concept\": \"JSP carrier twists: JSPX XML syntax, Java unicode escapes, includes across members\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"A timed/Mastery or host twist of D24: JSPX `<jsp:root xmlns:jsp=..>` with `<jsp:declaration>private static final String DESCRIPTOR_X = &quot;..&quot;;</jsp:declaration>` (XML entities, CDATA), `<jsp:scriptlet>`, `<jsp:\n  {\"id\": \"webshell-request-primitive-model\", \"concept\": \"webshell request/stage order and real-vs-inert execution primitives (D24 prompt; never asked yet)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D24 asked to 'recover the order of requests and stages, then separate the inert fixture behavior from the lines that would be real execution primitives' but shipped no handler code (D8 php_webshe\n  {\"id\": \"eex-heex-template-carrier\", \"concept\": \"Phoenix/Elixir templates as carriers (`.eex`/`.heex`/`.leex`, `~H` sigils, router/endpoint files)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D25's host was a bare controller module; a later host/timed twist could move the descriptor into `lib/<app>_web/templates/*.html.eex` (`<%= @descriptor %>`, `<%# HUNTRESS.. %>` EEx comments), HEEx `~H\\\"\n  {\"id\": \"game-archive-carriers\", \"concept\": \"other game archives as script carriers: Ren'Py `.rpa`/`.rpyc`, LÖVE `.love`, Unity TextAsset bundles, RPG Maker `plugins.js`\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"`.rpa` RPA-3.0 header `RPA-3.0 <hexoffset> <hexkey>` -> zlib-compressed pickle index (offset/len XOR key) -- parse with a RESTRICTED pickle reader that allows only dict/list/tupl\n  {\"id\": \"next-language-pool-roadmap\", \"concept\": \"read the timed plans' next_language pool as the forecast of upcoming languages\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D23 timed pool = 17 never-shipped languages incl. jsp; D24 shipped JSP and its pool lost exactly jsp; D24 pool had elixir, D25 shipped Elixir and its pool lost exactly elixir (2/2 hits). 15 left for 6 days: awk, beanshell, d\n  {\"id\": \"mastery-set-scope\", \"concept\": \"resolve every cross-file reference inside its own Mastery set\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D23 Mastery e24c070d: `4c1097.py` existed in all 7 sets; a bundle-wide index returned set1's handoff id for sets 2-7 (6 rejected). Index per inner evidence-0N.zip; cases must keep set-distinct values. D24: stems identical across all 8 sets again (`58\n  {\"id\": \"timed-contract-shape-diff\", \"concept\": \"diff the timed contract's id grammar against the single's before trusting the carried solver\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D23: single = semantic ids, timed = per-file hashed ids + composite fields; answered/asked dropped to 593/1495 and cost ~25 min across TT+Mastery. A pre-run check (answered ratio < 0.98 on a fresh contract => ge\n  {\"id\": \"solver-lib-v3-fallback\", \"concept\": \"carried solve.py must ask lib.codec.v3_plan when its own v=3 read yields nothing\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D19: lib.codec.v3_plan already decoded the ASPX escaped-nested carrier, but the carried solve.py `_v3` only used its own V3_MARK/descriptor regexes, so 11 ids went planless and the race harness probed guesses. The D20 solver-a\n  {\"id\": \"php-cli\", \"concept\": \"PHP CLI for lint/tokenize\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"sudo apt-get install -y php-cli  (php -l, token_get_all; never run fixtures). PHP is a carried language since D8.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"lua-unluac\", \"concept\": \"Lua interpreter + bytecode decompiler\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"sudo apt-get install -y lua5.4 luajit ; unluac.jar from https://sourceforge.net/projects/unluac/ into tools/unluac (java 25 installed) with bin/unluac wrapper. Needed if a luac-compiled carrier variant of the D9 Lua fixtures appears.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"xsltproc-cabextract-yq\", \"concept\": \"XML/CAB/YAML helpers\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"sudo apt-get install -y xsltproc cabextract ; yq: pip install yq into .venv (jq wrapper; jq installed). xsltproc only for --noout lint, never to apply a stylesheet.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"leaf-ext-list\", \"concept\": \"nested-zip sniff skips unknown leaf extensions\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"_LEAF_EXT in solve.py still lacks .lua .mof .ts .au3 .applescript .proj .pl .rb .ahk .gs .csx .groovy .yml .nsi .gd .jsp .exs (and future .tcl .r .kts .java .bsh .erl .ex .exs .nim .swift .fish .zsh .ipynb .go .rs .awk .tf .xsl .reg .inf .iss .wxs). Speed only (~1 s); \n  {\"id\": \"new-synthetic-label-family\", \"concept\": \"code-shape labels for a new language (D2-D7 style)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Polyglot days have been plan-verbatim since D8, but an 'advanced <lang>' set (like bash-advanced) would bring feature/primitive or control/style labels, and OLD label families can flip regime (batch expansion D15/D16). Apply playbook NAMING LAWS; probe\n  {\"id\": \"family-name-underscore\", \"concept\": \"host-type families like polyglot-github_actions / host-<profile>-<lang>\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Keep the longest-known-suffix field parse; derive the family prefix from the contract ids, never from the file stem (D14 msbuild_xml). D17 added `polyglot-auto_hotkey` (campaign AUTO_HOTKEY-, url host auto_hotkey-..). D18: `polyglot-go\n  {\"id\": \"godot-re-tools\", \"concept\": \"Godot pack/bytecode extractor\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"gdsdecomp (GDRE Tools) release binary into tools/gdre (headless: `gdre_tools --headless --recover=x.pck --output-dir=out`); only for .pck/.gdc/.exe Godot exports; never run the game. Static lib reader (godot-resource-pck-carrier) covers plain packs.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"unrpyc\", \"concept\": \"Ren'Py .rpyc decompiler\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"git clone https://github.com/CensoredUsername/unrpyc into tools/unrpyc; it unpickles (code execution risk) -- run only under python3 -I in the sandbox on copies, prefer the restricted lib reader.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"tcl-r-interpreters\", \"concept\": \"tclsh / Rscript for syntax checks\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"sudo apt-get install -y tcl (small); r-base-core is ~100 MB, install only on an R day. Static reading is enough for v=3 plans.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"applescript-scpt\", \"concept\": \"compiled AppleScript (.scpt FasdUAS) disassembly\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"git clone https://github.com/Jinmo/applescript-disassembler into tools/ (pure python). D13 shipped source .applescript only; a compiled variant would hide the marker in UTF-16/MacRoman strings.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"js-deob-extras\", \"concept\": \"synchrony / JSFuck decoding\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"npm i deobfuscator (synchrony CLI) into tools/npm; webcrack (installed) already handles obfuscator.io; JSFuck/JJencode via js_sandbox capture of the final call.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"ps-deob-modules\", \"concept\": \"PowerDecode / PSDecode for pwsh\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"git clone https://github.com/Malandrone/PowerDecode and https://github.com/R3MRUM/PSDecode into tools/ (pwsh 7.6.6 installed). refinery ps1 covers most; these add layer-by-layer IEX override tracing.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"xlm-standalone\", \"concept\": \"XLMMacroDeobfuscator CLI\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"uv pip install --python .venv/bin/python XLMMacroDeobfuscator  (refinery xlmdeobf is an inlined port and already works; standalone gives --sort-formulas/--extract-only).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"dotnet-script\", \"concept\": \"csx inspection\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"D19 shipped .csx source only (static read was enough). Install dotnet-script only if a csx variant needs `#load`/`#r` resolution: dotnet tool install --tool-path tools/dotnet-tools dotnet-script (parse only; ilspycmd covers compiled InstallUtil/MSBuild/Assembly.Load payloads).\"}\n]\n```","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fa8ad0f6-a2ad-4491-87fc-ff4325e1a9f3","uuid":"59c1d4e3-403c-47fd-8b46-992ce907868c","timestamp":"2026-10-26T13:05:57.740Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"## Readiness gaps\nBuilt by the nightly prebuild (dropped from the queue, still usable from lib/): D16-D23 nights (see git history) and D24 night\nper-file-hashed-contract, next-lang-pool-polyglot-battery, kotlin-beanshell-literal-route. Given up (2 attempts):\npython-exec-onion-static, evidence-type-router, file-registry-telemetry-reconcile, build-manifest-hooks,\nmacos-pkg-installer-scripts. Prebuild gate: lib imports limited to hctf/prebuil