h` with line-1 `# HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<B64|HEX|HB64|FRAG|LYR-..>-<data>` and each plausible descriptor form: zsh `typeset -r descriptor_<8hex>=\\\"..\\\"`, `readonly DESCRIPTOR_<8HEX>='..'`, `local -r`, `build_plan_<8hex>() { print -r -- \\\"..\\\" }` (function-return like D26 Erlang), `${(j::)parts}` joins of an array literal `parts=(..)`; fish `set -g descriptor_<8hex> \\\"..\\\"` (no `=`), `set -l`, `function build_plan_<8hex>; echo \\\"..\\\"; end`, `string join '' ..`. Assert lib.codec.v3_plan and the carried marker-routed solver return plan-verbatim language=zsh/fish, campaign ZSH-/FISH-<8hex>, host zsh-/fish-<10hex>.example.invalid, /tmp/huntress-<lang>/. Families `polyglot-zsh`/`polyglot-fish`. Stdlib only; never run zsh/fish.\"},\n {\"id\":\"awk-sed-minimal-v3-fixtures\",\"concept\":\"awk and sed v=3 polyglots in the plain D23-D26 shape (narrow re-queue of the given-up awk-sed-program-route)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"awk/sed are a sibling pair in the pool. awk-sed-program-route failed on a `__import__()` call (not allowed) and then on android xamarin_assembly_scan timing -- rebuild narrowly with plain imports. Fixtures: awk `#!/usr/bin/awk -f` + `# HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<TAG>-..` + `BEGIN { descriptor_<8hex> = \\\"..\\\" }` or `function build_plan_<8hex>() { return \\\"..\\\" }`, juxtaposition concat `\\\"ab\\\" \\\"cd\\\"`; sed `#!/bin/sed -f` / `#n` first line + `# HUNTRESS..` + `s/^.*$/<data>/` or `1i\\\\` / `a\\\\` text commands carrying the data, `y/abc/xyz/` transliteration. Assert marker-first plan recovery (data may contain `/` escaped as `\\\\/` inside s///) and plan-verbatim answers (language=awk/sed, AWK-/SED-<8hex>). Never run awk/sed on fixtures.\"},\n {\"id\":\"function-return-literal-battery\",\"concept\":\"nameless descriptor literals (function-return / command-argument) across the 14 remaining pool languages, plus a marker-damaged fallback\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"D22 NSIS (`StrCpy $0 \\\"..\\\"`) and D26 Erlang (`build_plan() -> \\\"<data>\\\".`) carried the data with NO descriptor name -- only the marker regex found it. A timed/next-day twist could split or drop the marker line. Prebuild a lib.codec fallback that collects every string literal >= 40 chars in any quote syntax (\\\"..\\\", '..', Tcl `{..}`, Lua `[[..]]`, heredocs, `r#\\\"..\\\"#`, Swift `#\\\"..\\\"#`, `\\\"\\\"\\\"..\\\"\\\"\\\"`), joins adjacent pieces, shape-peels each (max 4 layers) and accepts only `v=`; plus fixtures for each pool language's function-return form: Rust `fn build_plan() -> &'static str { \\\"..\\\" }`, Swift `func buildPlan() -> String { return \\\"..\\\" }`, Kotlin `fun buildPlan() = \\\"..\\\"`, BeanShell `String buildPlan() { return \\\"..\\\"; }`, Nim `proc buildPlan(): string = \\\"..\\\"`, Tcl `proc build_plan {} { return {..} }`, Makefile `define DESCRIPTOR`..`endef`, Dockerfile `LABEL huntress.descriptor=\\\"..\\\"`, XSLT `<xsl:variable name=\\\"d\\\" select=\\\"'..'\\\"/>`, HCL `output \\\"plan\\\" { value = \\\"..\\\" }`. Test: same plan with and without the marker line. Must stay inside the 2 s find_codecs fixture budget (gate on cheap substring/length tests).\"},\n {\"id\":\"cross-language-collision-decoys\",\"concept\":\"separate true cross-language indicators from deterministic collision decoys (D26 prompt; never asked yet)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"D26 prompt: 'some of its indicators look suspiciously familiar ... separate the true cross-language indicators from deterministic collision decoys planted to look like old friends'. No decoy shipped, but a later question family could ask e.g. `<fam>-<stem>-true-indicator` / `-decoy-count` / `-handoff-target`. Prebuild lib.codec.indicator_collisions(plans_by_member) for ONE Mastery set: index every url/host/campaign/file_path/next_stage/handoff_id value; a TRUE cross-language link = value (or campaign token) that matches the consuming file's own plan AND the producer's `next_language`/next_stage member; a DECOY = same shape/prefix as an older language's indicator (e.g. `cdn-<10hex>.example.invalid`, `PSPY-<16HEX>`) whose token differs from the file's campaign token, or whose `<lang>-` host prefix disagrees with `language=`. Return both lists with reasons; resolve per set (D23 lesson). Fixtures: two plans sharing a url host, one decoy differing in one hex char.\"},\n {\"id\":\"erlang-beam-chunk-literals\",\"concept\":\"compiled BEAM (`.beam`) and escript-archive carriers: recover string/binary literals statically\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"D26 shipped Erlang source only. A timed/host twist could ship the compiled module or an escript with an embedded archive (`#!/usr/bin/env escript` + `%%! -escript main x` + a zip/beam payload after the header lines). Parse `FOR1 <len> BEAM` IFF chunks with struct: `AtU8`/`Atom` atoms, `StrT` string table, `LitT` (4-byte uncompressed size + zlib) holding External Term Format literals (tags 107 STRING_EXT, 109 BINARY_EXT, 108 LIST_EXT, 97/98 ints, 104/105 tuples, 119/118 atoms) -- hand-roll an ETF reader, no erlang on box; for escript archives skip the first 3 text lines and open the rest with zipfile. Feed every recovered string to lib.codec.v3_plan. Stdlib only (struct, zlib, zipfile).\"},\n {\"id\":\"shell-rc-host-carriers\",\"concept\":\"shell startup/config files as v=3 HOST profiles for zsh/fish/bash (persistence-flavoured hosts)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"Hosts have shipped on web-flavoured days (D24 jsp_webshell, D25 elixir_phoenix) and none on D23/D26. If zsh/fish ship, a host is likely a startup file: `.zshrc`/`.zshenv`/`.zprofile`, oh-my-zsh `*.plugin.zsh`, `~/.config/fish/config.fish`, `conf.d/*.fish`, autoload `functions/<name>.fish`, bash `.bashrc`/`.profile` (T1546.004 Unix shell configuration modification). Expected host_profile spellings follow `<platform>_<kind>` (guess list for fixtures only: `zsh_rc`, `oh_my_zsh_plugin`, `fish_config`) -- answers stay plan-verbatim. Fixtures: marker + descriptor inside a function/alias/`precmd` hook, plus `source`/`autoload -Uz` lines that must be ignored. Assert routing by marker, not by file name.\"},\n {\"id\":\"jvm-pair-host-profiles\",\"concept\":\"BeanShell/Kotlin host carriers: JMeter `.jmx` samplers, Gradle Kotlin DSL, `.main.kts`\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"beanshell and kotlin are the JVM pair still in the pool (kotlin-beanshell-literal-route built the plain literal forms). Likely hosts: JMeter test plan XML `<BeanShellSampler>`/`<JSR223Sampler>` with `<stringProp name=\\\"BeanShellSampler.query\\\">` or `name=\\\"script\\\"` holding the script XML-escaped (`&quot;`, `&#xa;`) -> unescape then rescan (like D19 ASPX nesting); BeanShell in Burp/Ghidra/`bsh.Interpreter.eval(\\\"..\\\")`; Kotlin `build.gradle.kts`/`settings.gradle.kts` (`tasks.register(\\\"x\\\") { doLast { exec { commandLine(..) } } }`), `.main.kts` with `@file:DependsOn(..)`. Fixtures: marker in `<!-- -->` or `//`, descriptor escaped inside the XML property. Stdlib xml.etree only (never resolve entities from DTDs).\"},\n {\"id\":\"actor-message-flow-model\",\"concept\":\"actor/message-passing flow from source (Erlang/Elixir spawn-send-receive, workers, channels) -- D26 prompt\",\"priority\":3,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"D26 asked to 'trace the message flow' between processes; the fixture had no message code. If a later host ships it: static edge list from Erlang `Pid = spawn(fun ..)`/`spawn(M, F, A)`, `register(name, Pid)`, `Pid ! {Tag, Value}`, `receive {Tag, X} -> ..`, `gen_server:call/cast` + `handle_call/handle_cast`; Elixir `send(pid, msg)`, `GenServer.call`, `Task.async`; JS `postMessage`/`onmessage`; Go `ch <- v` / `<-ch`. Output ordered (sender, receiver, tag, payload) tuples and the final consumer of each indicator; answer-ids would likely be new suffixes -> lib.codec.plan_answer first. Regex-based, stdlib only; never run erl/elixir.\"},\n]\nnotes=[by[x] for x in [\"next-language-pool-roadmap\",\"mastery-set-scope\",\"timed-contract-shape-diff\",\"solver-lib-v3-fallback\"]]\nnl=by[\"next-language-pool-roadmap\"]\nnl[\"detail\"]=(\"3/3 hits: D23 pool had jsp -> D24 JSP; D24 pool had elixir -> D25 Elixir; D25 pool had erlang -> D26 Erlang; each day's pool lost exactly that language. \"\n  \"14 left for 5 days (D27-D31): awk, beanshell, dockerfile, fish, kotlin, makefile, nim, rust, sed, swift, tcl, terraform_hcl, xslt, zsh. \"\n  \"The last two drops were siblings (BEAM); remaining sibling pairs: zsh/fish, awk/sed, dockerfile/makefile, kotlin/beanshell. \"\n  \"Recompute nightly from every auto-* expected.json `-next-language` value and set the matching route gap to priority 1.\")\nrest=[g for g in old if g[\"id\"] not in drop and g[\"id\"] not in {\"nim-swift-tcl-literal-route\",\"stage-config-survival-diff\"} and g not in notes]\npb=[new[0],new[1],nst,new[2],new[3],new[4],new[5],new[6],scs,new[7]]\nout=pb+notes+rest\nids=[g[\"id\"] for g in out]; assert len(ids)==len(set(ids))\nfor g in out: assert set(g)=={\"id\",\"concept\",\"priority\",\"action\",\"detail\"},g[\"id\"]\nbody=\"[\\n\"+\",\\n\".join(\"  \"+json.dumps(g,ensure_ascii=False) for g in out)+\"\\n]\\n\"\nprose=\"\"\"## Readiness gaps\nBuilt by the nightly prebuild (dropped from the queue, still usable from lib/): D16-D24 nights (see git history) and D25 night\nfind-codecs-speed-gate, beam-erlang-elixir-route, rust-cargo-buildrs-route, terraform-hcl-function-fold, jsp-jspx-unicode-carrier,\nwebshell-request-primitive-model, eex-heex-template-carrier, game-archive-carriers. Given up (2 attempts): python-exec-onion-static,\nevidence-type-router, file-registry-telemetry-reconcile, macos-pkg-installer-scripts, zsh-fish-shell-route, awk-sed-program-route,\ncomposite-label-field-regime -- the D25-night failures were mostly OTHER lanes' fixture timings under load (android\nlocal_store_scan 4.67 s, xamarin_assembly_scan 2.05-6.10 s > 2 s) plus `__import__()` and `import tomllib` (not in\nhctf/prebuild.py ALLOWED_IMPORTS: use stdlib parsers already allowed, hand-roll TOML), so the pool-language pairs are\nre-queued under NEW narrow ids. Priority-1 order for D27: the pool sibling pairs (zsh/fish, awk/sed), the Nim/Swift/Tcl\nliteral forms, and the nameless-literal fallback (D22 NSIS + D26 Erlang had no descriptor name); then the D26 narrative\n(collision decoys), compiled BEAM, shell-rc and JVM host twists, the D25 config-survival model, message flow last.\n\n\"\"\"\ns=s[:i]+prose+\"```json\\n\"+body+s[k:]\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\npython3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json,re\ns=open('/home/testpwn/huntress-2026/reference/coverage/script-analysis.md').read()\ni=s.index(\"## Readiness gaps\"); j=s.index(\"```json\",i); k=s.index(\"```\",j+7)\ng=json.loads(s[j+7:k]); st=json.load(open('/home/testpwn/huntress-2026/.run/prebuild-state.json'))\npend=[x['id'] for x in g if x['action']=='prebuild' and not (st.get('script-analysis:'+x['id'],{}).get('ok') or st.get('script-analysis:'+x['id'],{}).get('attempts',0)>=2)]\nprint(len(g),len(pend),pend)\nprint(s[k:k+50])\nEOF\ntail -3 reference/coverage/script-analysis.md | cut -c1-80; wc -l reference/coverage/script-analysis.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1336,"cache_read_input_tokens":140009,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1336},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fa8ad0f6-a2ad-4491-87fc-ff4325e1a9f3","uuid":"43f41f22-4738-4aee-9490-f666be6bf9cf","timestamp":"2026-10-26T13:11:42.596Z","request_id":"req_011CgQuPv6Swaa9ruZKbX1Cr","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01AaFfKLLSWm2FP5o6HbTFaX":{"command":"cd /home/testpwn/huntress-2026; F=reference/coverage/script-analysis.md; python3 - \"$F\" <<'EOF'\nimport sys,json,re\np=sys.argv[1]; s=open(p).read()\ni=s.index(\"## Readiness gaps\"); j=s.index(\"```json\",i); k=s.index(\"```\",j+7)\nold=json.loads(s[j+7:k])\nby={g[\"id\"]:g for g in old}\ndrop={\"find-codecs-speed-gate\",\"beam-erlang-elixir-route\",\"zsh-fish-shell-route\",\"rust-cargo-buildrs-route\",\"awk-sed-program-route\",\n      \"terraform-hcl-function-fold\",\"composite-label-field-regime\",\"jsp-jspx-unicode-carrier\",\"webshell-request-primitive-model\",\n      \"eex-heex-template-carrier\",\"game-archive-carriers\"}\nnst=by[\"nim-swift-tcl-literal-route\"]; nst[\"priority\"]=1\nnst[\"detail\"]=(\"D26 night re-try (1st attempt failed ONLY on another lane's fixture timing: android/xam_blob_v1.json xamarin_assembly_scan 6.1 s under load). \"\n  \"3 of the 14 pool languages left after D26. \"+nst[\"detail\"])\nscs=by[\"stage-config-survival-diff\"]; scs[\"priority\"]=2\nscs[\"detail\"]=(\"1st attempt rejected: `import tomllib` is not in hctf/prebuild.py ALLOWED_IMPORTS -- hand-roll the TOML/sys.config/.exs keyword readers. \"+scs[\"detail\"])\nnew=[\n {\"id\":\"zsh-fish-minimal-v3-fixtures\",\"concept\":\"zsh and fish v=3 polyglots in the plain D23-D26 shape (narrow re-queue of the given-up zsh-fish-shell-route)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"zsh/fish are a sibling pair still in the 14-language pool after D26 (the last two drops were the BEAM pair Elixir -> Erlang). zsh-fish-shell-route failed twice ONLY on android fixture timing (local_store_scan 4.67 s), not on its own code -- rebuild narrowly: test fixtures `polyglot-zsh-{benign-utility,downloader,launcher,staged-chain}.zsh` and `polyglot-fish-*.fish` with line-1 `# HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<B64|HEX|HB64|FRAG|LYR-..>-<data>` and each plausible descriptor form: zsh `typeset -r descriptor_<8hex>=\\\"..\\\"`, `readonly DESCRIPTOR_<8HEX>='..'`, `local -r`, `build_plan_<8hex>() { print -r -- \\\"..\\\" }` (function-return like D26 Erlang), `${(j::)parts}` joins of an array literal `parts=(..)`; fish `set -g descriptor_<8hex> \\\"..\\\"` (no `=`), `set -l`, `function build_plan_<8hex>; echo \\\"..\\\"; end`, `string join '' ..`. Assert lib.codec.v3_plan and the carried marker-routed solver return plan-verbatim language=zsh/fish, campaign ZSH-/FISH-<8hex>, host zsh-/fish-<10hex>.example.invalid, /tmp/huntress-<lang>/. Families `polyglot-zsh`/`polyglot-fish`. Stdlib only; never run zsh/fish.\"},\n {\"id\":\"awk-sed-minimal-v3-fixtures\",\"concept\":\"awk and sed v=3 polyglots in the plain D23-D26 shape (narrow re-queue of the given-up awk-sed-program-route)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"awk/sed are a sibling pair in the pool. awk-sed-program-route failed on a `__import__()` call (not allowed) and then on android xamarin_assembly_scan timing -- rebuild narrowly with plain imports. Fixtures: awk `#!/usr/bin/awk -f` + `# HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<TAG>-..` + `BEGIN { descriptor_<8hex> = \\\"..\\\" }` or `function build_plan_<8hex>() { return \\\"..\\\" }`, juxtaposition concat `\\\"ab\\\" \\\"cd\\\"`; sed `#!/bin/sed -f` / `#n` first line + `# HUNTRESS..` + `s/^.*$/<data>/` or `1i\\\\` / `a\\\\` text commands carrying the data, `y/abc/xyz/` transliteration. Assert marker-first plan recovery (data may contain `/` escaped as `\\\\/` inside s///) and plan-verbatim answers (language=awk/sed, AWK-/SED-<8hex>). Never run awk/sed on fixtures.\"},\n {\"id\":\"function-return-literal-battery\",\"concept\":\"nameless descriptor literals (function-return / command-argument) across the 14 remaining pool languages, plus a marker-damaged fallback\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"D22 NSIS (`StrCpy $0 \\\"..\\\"`) and D26 Erlang (`build_plan() -> \\\"<data>\\\".`) carried the data with NO descriptor name -- only the marker regex found it. A timed/next-day twist could split or drop the marker line. Prebuild a lib.codec fallback that collects every string literal >= 40 chars in any quote syntax (\\\"..\\\", '..', Tcl `{..}`, Lua `[[..]]`, heredocs, `r#\\\"..\\\"#`, Swift `#\\\"..\\\"#`, `\\\"\\\"\\\"..\\\"\\\"\\\"`), joins adjacent pieces, shape-peels each (max 4 layers) and accepts only `v=`; plus fixtures for each pool language's function-return form: Rust `fn build_plan() -> &'static str { \\\"..\\\" }`, Swift `func buildPlan() -> String { return \\\"..\\\" }`, Kotlin `fun buildPlan() = \\\"..\\\"`, BeanShell `String buildPlan() { return \\\"..\\\"; }`, Nim `proc buildPlan(): string = \\\"..\\\"`, Tcl `proc build_plan {} { return {..} }`, Makefile `define DESCRIPTOR`..`endef`, Dockerfile `LABEL huntress.descriptor=\\\"..\\\"`, XSLT `<xsl:variable name=\\\"d\\\" select=\\\"'..'\\\"/>`, HCL `output \\\"plan\\\" { value = \\\"..\\\" }`. Test: same plan with and without the marker line. Must stay inside the 2 s find_codecs fixture budget (gate on cheap substring/length tests).\"},\n {\"id\":\"cross-language-collision-decoys\",\"concept\":\"separate true cross-language indicators from deterministic collision decoys (D26 prompt; never asked yet)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"D26 prompt: 'some of its indicators look suspiciously familiar ... separate the true cross-language indicators from deterministic collision decoys planted to look like old friends'. No decoy shipped, but a later question family could ask e.g. `<fam>-<stem>-true-indicator` / `-decoy-count` / `-handoff-target`. Prebuild lib.codec.indicator_collisions(plans_by_member) for ONE Mastery set: index every url/host/campaign/file_path/next_stage/handoff_id value; a TRUE cross-language link = value (or campaign token) that matches the consuming file's own plan AND the producer's `next_language`/next_stage member; a DECOY = same shape/prefix as an older language's indicator (e.g. `cdn-<10hex>.example.invalid`, `PSPY-<16HEX>`) whose token differs from the file's campaign token, or whose `<lang>-` host prefix disagrees with `language=`. Return both lists with reasons; resolve per set (D23 lesson). Fixtures: two plans sharing a url host, one decoy differing in one hex char.\"},\n {\"id\":\"erlang-beam-chunk-literals\",\"concept\":\"compiled BEAM (`.beam`) and escript-archive carriers: recover string/binary literals statically\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"D26 shipped Erlang source only. A timed/host twist could ship the compiled module or an escript with an embedded archive (`#!/usr/bin/env escript` + `%%! -escript main x` + a zip/beam payload after the header lines). Parse `FOR1 <len> BEAM` IFF chunks with struct: `AtU8`/`Atom` atoms, `StrT` string table, `LitT` (4-byte uncompressed size + zlib) holding External Term Format literals (tags 107 STRING_EXT, 109 BINARY_EXT, 108 LIST_EXT, 97/98 ints, 104/105 tuples, 119/118 atoms) -- hand-roll an ETF reader, no erlang on box; for escript archives skip the first 3 text lines and open the rest with zipfile. Feed every recovered string to lib.codec.v3_plan. Stdlib only (struct, zlib, zipfile).\"},\n {\"id\":\"shell-rc-host-carriers\",\"concept\":\"shell startup/config files as v=3 HOST profiles for zsh/fish/bash (persistence-flavoured hosts)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"Hosts have shipped on web-flavoured days (D24 jsp_webshell, D25 elixir_phoenix) and none on D23/D26. If zsh/fish ship, a host is likely a startup file: `.zshrc`/`.zshenv`/`.zprofile`, oh-my-zsh `*.plugin.zsh`, `~/.config/fish/config.fish`, `conf.d/*.fish`, autoload `functions/<name>.fish`, bash `.bashrc`/`.profile` (T1546.004 Unix shell configuration modification). Expected host_profile spellings follow `<platform>_<kind>` (guess list for fixtures only: `zsh_rc`, `oh_my_zsh_plugin`, `fish_config`) -- answers stay plan-verbatim. Fixtures: marker + descriptor inside a function/alias/`precmd` hook, plus `source`/`autoload -Uz` lines that must be ignored. Assert routing by marker, not by file name.\"},\n {\"id\":\"jvm-pair-host-profiles\",\"concept\":\"BeanShell/Kotlin host carriers: JMeter `.jmx` samplers, Gradle Kotlin DSL, `.main.kts`\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"beanshell and kotlin are the JVM pair still in the pool (kotlin-beanshell-literal-route built the plain literal forms). Likely hosts: JMeter test plan XML `<BeanShellSampler>`/`<JSR223Sampler>` with `<stringProp name=\\\"BeanShellSampler.query\\\">` or `name=\\\"script\\\"` holding the script XML-escaped (`&quot;`, `&#xa;`) -> unescape then rescan (like D19 ASPX nesting); BeanShell in Burp/Ghidra/`bsh.Interpreter.eval(\\\"..\\\")`; Kotlin `build.gradle.kts`/`settings.gradle.kts` (`tasks.register(\\\"x\\\") { doLast { exec { commandLine(..) } } }`), `.main.kts` with `@file:DependsOn(..)`. Fixtures: marker in `<!-- -->` or `//`, descriptor escaped inside the XML property. Stdlib xml.etree only (never resolve entities from DTDs).\"},\n {\"id\":\"actor-message-flow-model\",\"concept\":\"actor/message-passing flow from source (Erlang/Elixir spawn-send-receive, workers, channels) -- D26 prompt\",\"priority\":3,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"D26 asked to 'trace the message flow' between processes; the fixture had no message code. If a later host ships it: static edge list from Erlang `Pid = spawn(fun ..)`/`spawn(M, F, A)`, `register(name, Pid)`, `Pid ! {Tag, Value}`, `receive {Tag, X} -> ..`, `gen_server:call/cast` + `handle_call/handle_cast`; Elixir `send(pid, msg)`, `GenServer.call`, `Task.async`; JS `postMessage`/`onmessage`; Go `ch <- v` / `<-ch`. Output ordered (sender, receiver, tag, payload) tuples and the final consumer of each indicator; answer-ids would likely be new suffixes -> lib.codec.plan_answer first. Regex-based, stdlib only; never run erl/elixir.\"},\n]\nnotes=[by[x] for x in [\"next-language-pool-roadmap\",\"mastery-set-scope\",\"timed-contract-shape-diff\",\"solver-lib-v3-fallback\"]]\nnl=by[\"next-language-pool-roadmap\"]\nnl[\"detail\"]=(\"3/3 hits: D23 pool had jsp -> D24 JSP; D24 pool had elixir -> D25 Elixir; D25 pool had erlang -> D26 Erlang; each day's pool lost exactly that language. \"\n  \"14 left for 5 days (D27-D31): awk, beanshell, dockerfile, fish, kotlin, makefile, nim, rust, sed, swift, tcl, terraform_hcl, xslt, zsh. \"\n  \"The last two drops were siblings (BEAM); remaining sibling pairs: zsh/fish, awk/sed, dockerfile/makefile, kotlin/beanshell. \"\n  \"Recompute nightly from every auto-* expected.json `-next-language` value and set the matching route gap to priority 1.\")\nrest=[g for g in old if g[\"id\"] not in drop and g[\"id\"] not in {\"nim-swift-tcl-literal-route\",\"stage-config-survival-diff\"} and g not in notes]\npb=[new[0],new[1],nst,new[2],new[3],new[4],new[5],new[6],scs,new[7]]\nout=pb+notes+rest\nids=[g[\"id\"] for g in out]; assert len(ids)==len(set(ids))\nfor g in out: assert set(g)=={\"id\",\"concept\",\"priority\",\"action\",\"detail\"},g[\"id\"]\nbody=\"[\\n\"+\",\\n\".join(\"  \"+json.dumps(g,ensure_ascii=False) for g in out)+\"\\n]\\n\"\nprose=\"\"\"## Readiness gaps\nBuilt by the nightly prebuild (dropped from the queue, still usable from lib/): D16-D24 nights (see git history) and D25 night\nfind-codecs-speed-gate, beam-erlang-elixir-route, rust-cargo-buildrs-route, terraform-hcl-function-fold, jsp-jspx-unicode-carrier,\nwebshell-request-primitive-model, eex-heex-template-carrier, game-archive-carriers. Given up (2 attempts): python-exec-onion-static,\nevidence-type-router, file-registry-telemetry-reconcile, macos-pkg-installer-scripts, zsh-fish-shell-route, awk-sed-program-route,\ncomposite-label-field-regime -- the D25-night failures were mostly OTHER lanes' fixture timings under load (android\nlocal_store_scan 4.67 s, xamarin_assembly_scan 2.05-6.10 s > 2 s) plus `__import__()` and `import tomllib` (not in\nhctf/prebuild.py ALLOWED_IMPORTS: use stdlib parsers already allowed, hand-roll TOML), so the pool-language pairs are\nre-queued under NEW narrow ids. Priority-1 order for D27: the pool sibling pairs (zsh/fish, awk/sed), the Nim/Swift/Tcl\nliteral forms, and the nameless-literal fallback (D22 NSIS + D26 Erlang had no descriptor name); then the D26 narrative\n(collision decoys), compiled BEAM, shell-rc and JVM host twists, the D25 config-survival model, message flow last.\n\n\"\"\"\ns=s[:i]+prose+\"```json\\n\"+body+s[k:]\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\npython3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json,re\ns=open('/home/testpwn/huntress-2026/reference/coverage/script-analysis.md').read()\ni=s.index(\"## Readiness gaps\"); j=s.index(\"```json\",i); k=s.index(\"```\",j+7)\ng=json.loads(s[j+7:k]); st=json.load(open('/home/testpwn/huntress-2026/.run/prebuild-state.json'))\npend=[x['id'] for x in g if x['action']=='prebuild' and not (st.get('script-analysis:'+x['id'],{}).get('ok') or st.get('script-analysis:'+x['id'],{}).get('attempts',0)>=2)]\nprint(len(g),len(pend),pend)\nprint(s[k:k+50])\nEOF\ntail -3 reference/coverage/script-analysis.md | cut -c1-80; wc -l reference/coverage/script-analysis.md"}}}
